-- allium: 3
-- authentication.allium — who a request is, how they proved it, and the credentials they hold.
--
-- Scope: every way a party proves its identity to the forge, and every credential the
--   forge issues or trusts: registration and account activation, interactive sign-in
--   (password, second factor, remember-me, external identity providers, OpenID 2.0),
--   sign-out and sessions, password reset/change/policy, TOTP and WebAuthn second
--   factors and passkeys, personal access tokens and their scope taxonomy, request authentication
--   for the API / git / LFS (token or OAuth2 token as bearer or as the Basic-auth
--   password, HTTP signatures, reverse-proxy
--   headers, trusted external JWTs), the OAuth2/OIDC provider (applications, consent,
--   grants, codes, PKCE, refresh, introspection, userinfo), admin-managed external
--   authentication sources (LDAP, SMTP, PAM, OAuth2/OIDC, remote) with group mapping
--   and the scheduled directory sync, and linking external identities to accounts.
--
-- Includes: Session, LongTermAuthorization (remember-me), EmailVerificationCode
--   (account activation, password reset, secondary e-mail confirmation),
--   MailSendThrottle, UserLogin (which source verifies a user's password and the
--   must-change-password flag), TwoFactor (TOTP + scratch code), WebAuthnCredential,
--   AccessToken (+ TokenScope taxonomy and repository-specific tokens), AuthSource,
--   DirectoryEntry (external), ExternalLogin, OpenIDIdentity, OAuth2Application,
--   OAuth2Grant, OAuth2AuthorizationCode, OAuth2TokenIssuance, AuthorizedIntegration,
--   the CredentialPolicy contract other modules call (password policy, second-factor
--   facts, token scope categories, external-identity lookups).
--   The sync_external_users schedule is administration's CronTask; this module only
--   does the work (ScheduledExternalUserSync).
--
-- Excludes:
--   - SSPI (Windows integrated auth): removed from Forgejo; the source kind number is a
--     tombstone only.
--   - Gitea-compatibility headers (X-Gitea-OTP alongside X-Forgejo-OTP), the deprecated
--     `token`/`access_token` query parameters and the legacy "sudo" scope literal:
--     compatibility accidents, a rebuild needs one OTP header and header-only tokens.
--   - Password hash algorithm choice and silent re-hashing on sign-in: implementation.
--   - Token byte lengths, prefixes (gto_/gta_), lookup-key/validator split, LRU caches
--     of successful tokens, JWT signing key file locations: implementation.
--   - Actions runner/task tokens, Actions runtime tokens and LFS transfer tokens: these
--     credentials are minted and owned by actions.allium / code.allium; this module only
--     lists them as CredentialMethod values so access can tell them apart.
--   - SSH key authentication on the SSH transport: keys.allium / code.allium.
--   - Username syntax, reserved names, rename cooldown, e-mail uniqueness: accounts.allium
--     (called here as black-box checks).
--   - Admin user management (create user with must-change-password, activate, prohibit
--     login, delete): administration.allium / accounts.allium; this module only exposes
--     the fields they set.
--   - The orphaned-OAuth2-application doctor check: an operational repair tool.
--   - Remote/placeholder user promotion internals (RemoteSource matching migrated users on
--     first OAuth2 sign-in): left as one rule; the placeholder users themselves belong to
--     accounts.allium / migrations.allium.
--
-- Emits (other modules react):
--   UserSignedUp(user)                                   -> notifications (admin notice / welcome), accounts
--                                                           (this module is its only emitter: every
--                                                           registration path creates the accounts/User here)
--   UnconfirmedPrimaryEmailReplaced(user, new_address)   -> accounts (swap the primary EmailAddress row)
--   UserSignedIn(user, method)                           -> accounts (last-login), notifications
--   UserSignedOut(user, session)                         -> notifications (event stream "logout" to other tabs)
--   ActivationEmailRequested(user, code)                 -> notifications (MailMessage)
--   EmailConfirmationRequested(user, email, code)        -> notifications (MailMessage)
--   AccountActivated(user)                               -> accounts, notifications
--   EmailConfirmationLinkFollowed(user, email)           -> accounts (EmailAddress.is_activated)
--   PasswordResetRequested(user, code)                   -> notifications (MailMessage)
--   PasswordChanged(user)                                -> notifications (security mail)
--   TotpEnrolled(user) / TotpDisabled(user)              -> notifications (security mail)
--   SecurityKeyRemoved(user, name)                       -> notifications (security mail)
--   ExternalGroupsAsserted(user, source, groups)         -> organizations (team mapping)
--   ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted(user, source, groups)    -> quota (quota-group mapping): the OAuth2
--                                                           quota-group claim, or the LDAP entry's
--                                                           groups (decided: requests 6)
--   ExternalSshKeysAsserted(user, source, keys)          -> keys (source-managed SSH keys)
--   ExternalAvatarAsserted(user, url)                    -> accounts (avatar upload)
--   ExternalAdminFlagsAsserted(user, is_admin, is_restricted) -> accounts
--   RequestAuthenticated(user, method)                   -> access (scope/repository reducers), accounts (token last use)
--   PasswordBasicAuthRefused(request)                    -> (web layer: 401 "use a token")
--   AuthSourceDeleted(source)                            -> organizations (clear team-membership provenance)
--   (PasswordChanged(user) is also emitted when an administrator or the operator sets
--    a password: administration/UserPasswordSetByAdmin, UserPasswordSetByOperator)
--   OAuth2ProviderRedirectRequested(session, source, prompt_none) -> (web layer: redirect to IdP)
--   ConsentRequested(user, app, redirect_uri, scopes)    -> (web layer: render the consent page)
--   AuthorizationDenied(user, app)                       -> (web layer: redirect with error=access_denied)
--   ClientSecretRegenerated(app)                         -> (web layer: show the new secret once)
--   ExternalUserSyncRefused(source)                      -> administration (a system notice: the directory
--                                                           returned nobody and deactivating all is off)
--   AuthSourceSyncRequested(source, update_existing)     -> (internal: per-source sync; LDAP handled here)
--   RemoteUserClaimed(user, email)                       -> accounts (promote the F3 placeholder)
--
--   ExternalUserSyncFinished()          -- administration: the sync_external_users run is done
-- Reacts to:
--   accounts/UserEmailAdded(user, address)     -- issue a confirmation code for a new address
--   accounts/EmailActivationRequested(user, address) -- re-issue it (resend)
--   accounts/PrimaryEmailChanged(user, old_address, new_address) -- old codes and remember-me die
--   accounts/UserPurged(user)                  -- end every session at once
--   accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, kind, purge, delete_contributions) -- drop every credential
--   administration/InstanceStarted(instance)   -- reconcile the built-in OAuth2 applications
--   administration/ExternalUserSyncDue(update_existing) -- the sync_external_users cron task
--   administration/UserTwoFactorResetByAdmin(admin, user)  -- drop every second factor
--   administration/UserLoginSourceSetByAdmin(admin, user, login_source, login_name) -- rebind the UserLogin
--   administration/UserPasswordSetByAdmin(admin, user, password),
--   administration/UserPasswordSetByOperator(operator, user, password) -- remember-me dies, security mail
--   administration/AccessTokenRequestedForUser(requester, user, token_name, scopes) -- admin API / CLI token
--   administration/AuthorizedIntegrationRequested(operator, user, name, description, issuer, claim_rules, scopes, all_repositories, repositories)
--   administration/AuthSourceConfiguredFromCli(operator, kind, action, source, name, is_active, sync_enabled, settings)
--
-- Read-only mode: every user-initiated write of this module (registration, activation,
--   linking, password, second-factor, token, integration and application management)
--   is refused while access/InstanceWriteGate.read_only (decided: administration 3).
--   Signing in and out, remember-me, request authentication and the OAuth2 provider's
--   authorize / consent / token flow keep working: they are how people reach the
--   instance to read it. Site-admin and operator actions are not gated (the admin
--   console stays writable).

use "./accounts.allium" as accounts
use "./organizations.allium" as organizations
use "./repositories.allium" as repositories
use "./access.allium" as access
use "./keys.allium" as keys
use "./administration.allium" as administration

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- What an external identity provider (OAuth2/OIDC source) told us about the person who
-- just came back from it. Held in the session while the person decides to link or
-- register.
-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:1556
value ExternalIdentity {
    source: AuthSource
    external_id: String                 -- the provider's stable user id ("sub")
    email: String?
    email_verified: Boolean             -- the IdP asserted email_verified = true
    nickname: String?
    preferred_username: String?
    full_name: String?
    avatar_url: String?
    groups: Set<String>                 -- values of the source's group claim
    quota_groups: Set<String>           -- values of the source's quota-group claim
    ssh_public_keys: Set<String>        -- values of the source's SSH-key attribute
    claim_names: Set<String>            -- every claim name present
}

-- One rule an AuthorizedIntegration applies to a presented JWT's claims.
-- from: models/auth/authorized_integration.go:116
value ClaimRule {
    claim: String
    comparison: ClaimComparison
    value: String?                      -- for eq / glob
    values: Set<String>                 -- for in / glob_in
    nested: List<ClaimRule>             -- for nest: rules applied inside an object claim
}

-- Kind-specific settings of an authentication source. Only the group for the source's
-- kind is meaningful.
-- from: services/auth/source/ldap/source.go:25
value AuthSourceSettings {
    -- LDAP (bind DN search, or direct "simple" bind)
    host: String?
    port: Integer?
    security_protocol: LdapSecurityProtocol?
    skip_tls_verify: Boolean
    bind_dn: String?                    -- bind_dn mode: service account used to search
    user_base: String?                  -- search base
    user_dn_template: String?           -- simple mode: DN template with the login substituted
    user_filter: String?                -- entry must match to be allowed to sign in
    admin_filter: String?               -- entry matching makes the user a site admin
    restricted_filter: String?          -- entry matching makes the user restricted
    attribute_username: String?
    attribute_first_name: String?
    attribute_surname: String?
    attribute_mail: String?
    attribute_ssh_public_key: String?
    attribute_avatar: String?
    attributes_in_bind: Boolean
    search_page_size: Integer?
    allow_deactivate_all: Boolean       -- an empty directory listing may deactivate everyone
    groups_enabled: Boolean
    group_dn: String?
    group_filter: String?
    group_member_attribute: String?
    user_uid_attribute: String?
    -- SMTP
    smtp_auth: SmtpAuthKind?
    smtp_allowed_domains: Set<String>
    force_smtps: Boolean
    helo_hostname: String?
    disable_helo: Boolean
    -- PAM
    pam_service_name: String?
    pam_email_domain: String?
    -- OAuth2 / OIDC
    provider: String?                   -- e.g. openidConnect, github, gitlab, gitea, nextcloud, ...
    client_id: String?
    openid_discovery_url: String?
    custom_urls: Set<String>            -- auth/token/profile/email URLs for self-hosted providers
    icon_url: String?
    scopes: Set<String>
    required_claim_name: String?        -- sign-in refused unless the claim is present
    required_claim_value: String?       -- ...and contains this value
    group_claim_name: String?
    admin_group: String?                -- membership makes the user a site admin
    restricted_group: String?           -- membership makes the user restricted
    group_team_map: String?             -- JSON {group: {org: [team, ...]}}
    group_team_map_removal: Boolean     -- remove from mapped teams when the group is gone
    dynamic_group_maps: String?
    dynamic_group_maps_removal: Boolean
    quota_group_claim_name: String?
    quota_group_map: String?
    quota_group_map_removal: Boolean
    allow_username_change: Boolean
    -- Remote (placeholder users promoted on first external sign-in)
    remote_url: String?
    remote_matching_source: String?
    -- All kinds
    skip_local_two_factor: Boolean      -- trust the source's own 2FA; skip local TOTP/WebAuthn
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

-- What a password-verifying source must do when the forge hands it a login and a
-- password. Local (no source), LDAP, SMTP and PAM all fulfil it.
contract PasswordAuthenticator {
    authenticate: (source: AuthSource, login_name: String, password: String) -> DirectoryEntry

    @invariant NoEnumeration
        -- A wrong password, an unknown login, an unactivated e-mail address and a
        -- login-prohibited account are indistinguishable to the caller except that a
        -- prohibited account is told so after the password matched.

    @invariant AutoProvision
        -- LDAP, SMTP and PAM sources create an active local account on the first
        -- successful bind of an unknown login (SMTP: name = local part of the address;
        -- PAM: e-mail = login@pam_email_domain).
}

-- An external OpenID Connect issuer whose JWTs an AuthorizedIntegration trusts.
contract TrustedIssuer {
    discovery: (issuer: String) -> String
    signing_keys: (issuer: String) -> Set<String>

    @invariant SameHostKeys
        -- The discovery document's issuer must equal the configured issuer exactly, it
        -- must advertise signing algorithms and a JWKS URI, and the JWKS URI must be on
        -- the issuer's own host. Only asymmetric algorithms are accepted.

    @invariant InternalIssuersNeedNoFetch
        -- Issuers the forge runs itself (Actions OIDC tokens at <app-url>/api/actions)
        -- are verified with the forge's own key and stored under a placeholder issuer
        -- so a change of the instance URL does not break stored integrations.
}

-- What other modules ask of authentication. Each module calls these as local
-- black boxes (password_acceptable(password), has_two_factor(user), ...) and maps
-- them in its header to the function here, as with access/AuthorizationPolicy.
contract CredentialPolicy {
    -- The password policy every path that sets a password applies (sign-up,
    -- reset, change, admin create / set, CLI): at least config.min_password_length
    -- characters, one of each class in config.password_complexity, and, when
    -- config.password_check_pwned is on, not in the HaveIBeenPwned list
    -- (k-anonymity range query; a failing lookup refuses the password).
    -- from: modules/auth/password/password.go:60, services/user/update.go:172
    password_acceptable: (password: String) -> Boolean
    -- The length part alone (the install wizard's first administrator).
    password_long_enough: (password: String) -> Boolean
    -- The password authenticates the account through its UserLogin source (local
    -- store, LDAP, SMTP, PAM); false when the account has no password. Used for
    -- re-entering the password before a sensitive act (accounts' own deletion).
    -- from: routers/web/user/setting/account.go:277
    password_matches: (user: accounts/User, password: String) -> Boolean
    -- The source the account signs in through: UserLogin{user}.source, null for
    -- a local account (decided: requests 4; accounts/User.login_source reads it).
    login_source_of: (user: accounts/User) -> AuthSource?
    -- UserLogin{user}.has_second_factor: TOTP or any WebAuthn credential enrolled.
    has_two_factor: (user: accounts/User) -> Boolean
    -- UserLogin{user}.requires_two_factor (config.global_two_factor_requirement).
    must_have_two_factor: (user: accounts/User) -> Boolean
    -- The request was authenticated with the account password. Never true:
    -- password Basic auth is refused everywhere (decided: authentication 4,
    -- ClientPasswordBasicAuthRefused), so callers may keep the check as a guard.
    authenticated_by_password: (user: accounts/User) -> Boolean
    -- Does a credential's scope set admit a request of this category and level?
    -- Write implies read in the same category; no scope of the category refuses.
    -- Only tokens, OAuth2 grants with token scopes and authorized integrations
    -- are scoped; a session is never scope-checked.
    -- from: models/auth/access_token_scope.go:300
    scope_allows: (scopes: Set<TokenScope>, category: ScopeCategory, level: ScopeLevel) -> Boolean
    -- The local account holding an ExternalLogin whose provider speaks
    -- `source_kind`, whose source authenticates against `host` (provider_host)
    -- and whose external_id equals `external_id` as a string; null when none.
    -- The OAuth2 source's name plays no part (migrations' re-attribution).
    linked_account_for: (source_kind: String, host: String, external_id: String) -> accounts/User?
    -- The forge kind an OAuth2 provider type speaks (migrations' source kinds:
    -- github, gitlab, gitea, forgejo, ...); null for providers that are not a
    -- forge (Google, Discord, generic OpenID Connect, ...).
    source_kind_for_provider: (provider: String) -> String?
    -- The host an OAuth2 source authenticates against: the host of its custom
    -- URLs when set (self-hosted), otherwise the provider's public host
    -- (github.com, gitlab.com, ...).
    provider_host: (source: AuthSource) -> String
    -- Teams a source's group mapping puts a user in: settings.group_team_map
    -- ({group: {org: [team...]}}) plus settings.dynamic_group_maps, for the
    -- groups the user is in. Mapped organizations or teams that do not exist
    -- are skipped.
    teams_mapped_from: (source: AuthSource, groups: Set<String>) -> Set<organizations/Team>
    -- Teams mapped from groups the user is NOT in, which they leave; empty
    -- unless settings.group_team_map_removal (or dynamic_group_maps_removal).
    teams_unmapped_from: (source: AuthSource, user: accounts/User, groups: Set<String>) -> Set<organizations/Team>

    @invariant ActivityPubNeedsItsScope
        -- Federation's activitypub routes accept a scoped credential only with
        -- read_activitypub (GET) or write_activitypub (POST to an inbox).
        -- Routes addressed by user id honour a public_only credential: a
        -- private or limited user answers as not found.

    @invariant RouteFamiliesNameTheirCategory
        -- Each API route family names one category: /admin -> admin,
        -- /activitypub -> activitypub, /notifications -> notification,
        -- /orgs and /teams -> organization, /packages -> package,
        -- /repos/../issues and /pulls conversation routes -> issue, other /repos
        -- -> repository, /user and /users -> user, everything else -> misc.
        -- GET / HEAD need read, every other method needs write
        -- (access.allium's authorization table column "scope").
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The category part of a TokenScope; the level is ScopeLevel.
-- from: models/auth/access_token_scope.go:18
enum ScopeCategory { activitypub | admin | misc | notification | organization | package | issue | repository | user }
enum ScopeLevel { read | write }

-- from: models/auth/source.go:21
enum AuthSourceKind { ldap_bind_dn | ldap_simple | smtp | pam | oauth2 | remote }

-- from: services/auth/source/ldap/security_protocol.go:11
enum LdapSecurityProtocol { unencrypted | ldaps | start_tls }

-- from: services/auth/source/smtp/auth.go:45
enum SmtpAuthKind { plain | login | cram_md5 }

-- Every personal-access-token scope. Write implies read in the same category.
-- `all` on input expands to every write scope; `public-only` is a separate flag.
-- from: models/auth/access_token_scope.go:53
enum TokenScope {
    read_activitypub | write_activitypub
    | read_admin | write_admin
    | read_misc | write_misc
    | read_notification | write_notification
    | read_organization | write_organization
    | read_package | write_package
    | read_issue | write_issue
    | read_repository | write_repository
    | read_user | write_user
}

-- How a request proved who it is.
-- from: services/auth/interface.go:26
enum CredentialMethod {
    -- decided: no password_basic method: username+password Basic auth is refused on
    -- every route (API, git, LFS); tokens and OAuth2 tokens only.
    session | access_token | oauth2_bearer | http_signature
    | reverse_proxy | integration_jwt | actions_task_token | actions_runtime_token | lfs_token
}

-- How an interactive sign-in completed.
enum SignInMethod { password_login | totp | scratch_code | webauthn | passkey | remember_me | external_provider | openid | reverse_proxy | activation | password_reset }

-- from: models/auth/auth_token.go:20
enum VerificationPurpose { user_activation | password_reset | email_activation }

-- from: modules/setting/service.go:22
enum CaptchaKind { image | recaptcha | hcaptcha | mcaptcha | cfturnstile }

-- from: modules/auth/password/password.go:36
enum PasswordCharacterClass { lower | upper | digit | spec }

-- from: modules/setting/security.go:548
enum TwoFactorRequirement { none | all | admin }

-- from: modules/setting/oauth2.go:14
enum ExternalUsernameSource { userid | nickname | email | preferred_username }

-- from: modules/setting/oauth2.go:30
enum AccountLinkingMode { disabled | login | auto }

-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:428
enum PkceMethod { s256 | plain | none }

-- from: models/auth/authorized_integration.go:131
enum ClaimComparison { eq | in | glob | glob_in | nest }

-- from: models/auth/authorized_integration.go:142
enum IntegrationUi { generic | forgejo_actions_local }

-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:59
enum BuiltinOAuth2App { git_credential_oauth | git_credential_manager | tea }

-- What a site administrator's mail-throttle protects. `resend` is the throttle shared by
-- activation resends and password-reset mails; `password_reset` is used for reset mails
-- only when config.mail_throttle_shared is off.
enum ThrottleKind { resend | password_reset | email_change }

enum SessionStatus { anonymous | pending_second_factor | authenticated | destroyed }
enum RememberMeStatus { active | consumed | revoked | expired }
enum VerificationCodeStatus { pending | used | expired | revoked }
-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:415
enum AuthorizationCodeStatus { issued | redeemed | expired }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A browser session. Every web visitor has one; it becomes authenticated by a sign-in.
-- from: models/auth/session.go:17
entity Session {
    status: SessionStatus
    user: accounts/User?                        -- set once authenticated
    authenticated_via: SignInMethod?
    pending_user: accounts/User?                -- passed the first factor, owes a second
    remember_requested: Boolean                 -- issue a remember-me cookie on completion
    pending_sso_source: AuthSource?             -- remember-me after 2FA is bound to this IdP
    pending_external_identity: ExternalIdentity?  -- came back from an IdP, not yet linked
    pending_link: Boolean                       -- link pending_external_identity after 2FA
    pending_openid_uri: String?                 -- link this OpenID after 2FA
    remember_me: LongTermAuthorization?         -- the remember-me record this browser holds
    last_activity_at: Timestamp

    is_signed_in: status = authenticated

    transitions status {
        anonymous -> pending_second_factor
        anonymous -> authenticated
        pending_second_factor -> authenticated
        anonymous -> destroyed
        pending_second_factor -> destroyed
        authenticated -> destroyed
        terminal: destroyed
    }
}

-- The "remember me" credential: survives the session, re-establishes it on the next
-- visit. The SSO variant is bound to an OAuth2 source and, instead of signing in
-- directly, sends the browser through a silent (prompt=none) re-authentication at that
-- provider, so a user disabled at the IdP is not kept signed in.
-- from: models/auth/auth_token.go:31
entity LongTermAuthorization {
    user: accounts/User
    sso_source: AuthSource?
    expires_at: Timestamp
    status: RememberMeStatus

    is_sso: sso_source != null

    transitions status {
        active -> consumed
        active -> revoked
        active -> expired
        terminal: consumed, revoked, expired
    }
}

-- A one-time code mailed to a user: activate the account, reset the password, or
-- confirm an additional e-mail address.
-- from: models/auth/auth_token.go:31
entity EmailVerificationCode {
    user: accounts/User
    purpose: VerificationPurpose
    email: String?                      -- the address being confirmed (email_activation)
    expires_at: Timestamp
    status: VerificationCodeStatus

    -- Expiry is applied by VerificationCodeExpires, so a pending code is a live one.
    is_valid: status = pending

    transitions status {
        pending -> used
        pending -> expired
        pending -> revoked
        terminal: used, expired, revoked
    }
}

-- "You asked for a mail very recently." Rate-limits activation resends, password reset
-- mails and unconfirmed-address changes per user.
-- from: routers/web/auth/auth.go:687
entity MailSendThrottle {
    user: accounts/User
    kind: ThrottleKind
    until: Timestamp
}

-- How a user's password is verified and whether they must change it.
-- One per user. source = null means the forge's own password store.
-- from: models/user/user.go:75
entity UserLogin {
    user: accounts/User
    source: AuthSource?
    login_name: String                  -- the name the source knows the user by
    has_password: Boolean               -- a local password is set (OAuth2 users may have none)
    must_change_password: Boolean
    password_changed_at: Timestamp?
    last_sign_in_at: Timestamp?

    is_local: source = null
    may_reset_password: is_local or (source.kind = oauth2 and has_password)
    has_totp: exists TwoFactor{user: user}
    has_security_keys: exists WebAuthnCredential{user: user}
    has_second_factor: has_totp or has_security_keys
    skips_local_two_factor: source != null and source.settings.skip_local_two_factor
    requires_two_factor: user.kind = individual and (config.global_two_factor_requirement = all or (config.global_two_factor_requirement = admin and user.is_admin))
    -- The gate every authenticated request passes through (web shows the activation,
    -- prohibited, change-password or enrol-2FA page instead; API answers forbidden).
    -- An account being purged (accounts/User.being_purged) is refused everywhere.
    may_use_account: user.is_active and not user.prohibit_login and not user.being_purged and not must_change_password and (requires_two_factor = false or has_second_factor)
}

-- TOTP second factor. One per user. The scratch code is a single-use recovery code that
-- is replaced every time it is used.
-- from: models/auth/twofactor.go:46
entity TwoFactor {
    user: accounts/User
    last_used_passcode: String?          -- a passcode is accepted at most once
    scratch_code_generation: Integer     -- bumps whenever a new scratch code is issued
    enrolled_at: Timestamp
}

-- A WebAuthn security key or passkey. Every credential works as a second factor; a
-- passkey (discoverable credential) also signs its user in on its own.
-- from: models/auth/webauthn.go:44
entity WebAuthnCredential {
    user: accounts/User
    name: String                         -- unique per user, case-insensitive
    discoverable: Boolean                -- decided: a passkey, usable for passwordless sign-in
    sign_count: Integer
    backup_eligible: Boolean
    backup_state: Boolean
    created_at: Timestamp
}

-- A personal access token. The secret is shown once at creation/regeneration; only the
-- last eight characters are shown afterwards.
-- from: models/auth/access_token.go:59
entity AccessToken {
    owner: accounts/User
    name: String                         -- unique per owner, max 255
    scopes: Set<TokenScope>
    public_only: Boolean                 -- may only see public orgs/repos/users
    all_repositories: Boolean            -- false: only `repositories` are reachable
    repositories: Set<repositories/Repository>
    last_eight: String
    created_at: Timestamp
    last_used_at: Timestamp?

    has_been_used: last_used_at != null
    has_recent_activity: last_used_at != null and last_used_at + 7.days > now
}

-- An authentication source configured by a site administrator.
-- from: models/auth/source.go:99
entity AuthSource {
    name: String                         -- unique, max 30; the OAuth2 callback path uses it
    kind: AuthSourceKind
    is_active: Boolean
    sync_enabled: Boolean                -- only meaningful for LDAP sources
    settings: AuthSourceSettings
    created_at: Timestamp

    is_ldap: kind in {ldap_bind_dn, ldap_simple}
    provides_ssh_keys: (is_ldap or kind = oauth2) and settings.attribute_ssh_public_key != null
    allows_username_change: kind = oauth2 and settings.allow_username_change
    -- Quota-group mapping (quota.allium reads these). The map and its removal flag
    -- apply to every group-capable source, LDAP included (decided: quota 8); the
    -- claim name is OAuth2 only, LDAP groups come from the directory entry.
    quota_group_claim_name: settings.quota_group_claim_name
    quota_group_map: settings.quota_group_map
    quota_group_map_removal: settings.quota_group_map_removal
    verifies_passwords: kind in {ldap_bind_dn, ldap_simple, smtp, pam}
    logins: UserLogin with source = this
    external_logins: ExternalLogin with source = this
    in_use: logins.count > 0 or external_logins.count > 0
}

-- An entry in an LDAP directory, as the source's search returns it.
-- from: services/auth/source/ldap/source_search.go:21
external entity DirectoryEntry {
    source: AuthSource
    username: String
    email: String                       -- <username>@localhost.local when the directory has none
    first_name: String?
    surname: String?
    is_admin: Boolean
    is_restricted: Boolean
    ssh_public_keys: Set<String>
    groups: Set<String>
}

-- A link between a local account and an identity at an OAuth2/OIDC source.
-- from: models/user/external_login_user.go:59
entity ExternalLogin {
    user: accounts/User
    source: AuthSource
    external_id: String
    provider: String
    email: String?
    name: String?
    nickname: String?
    avatar_url: String?
    linked_at: Timestamp
}

-- An OpenID 2.0 identifier attached to an account.
-- from: models/user/openid.go:19
entity OpenIDIdentity {
    user: accounts/User
    uri: String                           -- normalised claimed identifier, globally unique
    show_publicly: Boolean
}

-- A client registered with the forge's OAuth2/OIDC provider.
-- Exactly one of owner_user / owner_org, or neither for instance-wide applications
-- (managed by site admins, including the built-in public clients).
-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:31
entity OAuth2Application {
    owner_user: accounts/User?
    owner_org: organizations/Organization?
    builtin: BuiltinOAuth2App?            -- a locked, configuration-managed public client
    name: String                          -- max 255
    client_id: String                     -- unique, generated
    confidential: Boolean                 -- confidential clients hold a client secret
    redirect_uris: Set<String>
    created_at: Timestamp

    is_instance_wide: owner_user = null and owner_org = null
    is_builtin: builtin != null
    grants: OAuth2Grant with application = this
}

-- A user's standing consent for an application. One per (user, application).
-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:471
entity OAuth2Grant {
    user: accounts/User
    application: OAuth2Application
    scopes: Set<String>                   -- openid/profile/email/groups plus optional token scopes
    nonce: String?
    counter: Integer                      -- refresh-token generation; a used refresh token is dead
    created_at: Timestamp

    -- Token scopes (beyond openid/profile/email/groups) narrow what the issued access
    -- tokens may do; with none, the tokens carry every scope.
    restricts_token_scopes: grant_token_scopes(scopes).count > 0
}

-- A one-time authorization code handed to the client via the redirect URI.
-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:381
entity OAuth2AuthorizationCode {
    grant: OAuth2Grant
    redirect_uri: String
    code_challenge: String?
    pkce_method: PkceMethod
    issued_at: Timestamp
    expires_at: Timestamp
    status: AuthorizationCodeStatus

    transitions status {
        issued -> redeemed
        issued -> expired
        terminal: redeemed, expired
    }
}

-- One response from the token endpoint: a signed access token, a refresh token tied to
-- the grant's counter, and (with the openid scope) an id_token.
-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:160
entity OAuth2TokenIssuance {
    grant: OAuth2Grant
    scopes: Set<String>                   -- the grant's scopes when issued; kept until refreshed
    refresh_counter: Integer
    access_expires_at: Timestamp
    refresh_expires_at: Timestamp
    includes_id_token: Boolean
    issued_at: Timestamp

    access_valid: access_expires_at > now
    refresh_usable: refresh_expires_at > now and (not config.oauth2_invalidate_refresh_tokens or (refresh_counter = grant.counter and refresh_counter > 0))
}

-- An external system whose JWTs the forge accepts as API credentials for `owner`
-- (e.g. a CI job's OIDC token). Looked up by exact (issuer, audience).
-- from: models/auth/authorized_integration.go:30
entity AuthorizedIntegration {
    owner: accounts/User
    name: String
    description: String?
    ui: IntegrationUi
    issuer: String
    audience: String
    claim_rules: List<ClaimRule>
    scopes: Set<TokenScope>
    public_only: Boolean
    all_repositories: Boolean
    repositories: Set<repositories/Repository>
    created_at: Timestamp
}

-- The scheduled "synchronise external user data" job is administration's CronTask
-- sync_external_users (schedule, enablement, last run); this module keeps no copy
-- of it and reacts to its ExternalUserSyncDue.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- [service] registration
    disable_registration: Boolean = false                       -- DISABLE_REGISTRATION
    allow_only_internal_registration: Boolean = false           -- ALLOW_ONLY_INTERNAL_REGISTRATION
    allow_only_external_registration: Boolean = false           -- ALLOW_ONLY_EXTERNAL_REGISTRATION (both on = registration disabled)
    show_registration_button: Boolean = true                    -- SHOW_REGISTRATION_BUTTON (default: registration open)
    register_email_confirm: Boolean = false                     -- REGISTER_EMAIL_CONFIRM
    register_manual_confirm: Boolean = false                    -- REGISTER_MANUAL_CONFIRM (ignored when email confirm is on)
    email_domain_allowlist: Set<String> = {}                    -- EMAIL_DOMAIN_ALLOWLIST (globs)
    email_domain_blocklist: Set<String> = {}                    -- EMAIL_DOMAIN_BLOCKLIST (globs)
    email_domain_block_disposable: Boolean = false              -- EMAIL_DOMAIN_BLOCK_DISPOSABLE
    enable_captcha: Boolean = false                             -- ENABLE_CAPTCHA
    captcha_kind: CaptchaKind = image                           -- CAPTCHA_TYPE
    require_captcha_for_login: Boolean = false                  -- REQUIRE_CAPTCHA_FOR_LOGIN
    require_external_registration_captcha: Boolean = false      -- REQUIRE_EXTERNAL_REGISTRATION_CAPTCHA (default = ENABLE_CAPTCHA)
    require_external_registration_password: Boolean = false     -- REQUIRE_EXTERNAL_REGISTRATION_PASSWORD
    default_user_is_restricted: Boolean = false                 -- DEFAULT_USER_IS_RESTRICTED
    activation_code_lifetime: Duration = 180.minutes            -- ACTIVE_CODE_LIVE_MINUTES
    reset_code_lifetime: Duration = 180.minutes                 -- RESET_PASSWD_CODE_LIVE_MINUTES; decided: reset links honour it
    mail_resend_interval: Duration = 3.minutes                  -- hard-coded 180 s throttle
    mail_throttle_shared: Boolean = true                        -- decided (new setting): one throttle for activation and reset mails (Forgejo); false = one per kind
    mail_service_configured: Boolean = false                    -- [mailer] ENABLED

    -- [service] sign-in
    enable_internal_signin: Boolean = true                      -- ENABLE_INTERNAL_SIGNIN
    require_signin_view: Boolean = false                        -- REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW
    -- decided: ENABLE_BASIC_AUTHENTICATION is gone; password Basic auth is never accepted
    -- and a token or OAuth2 token in the Basic password is always accepted (git needs it).
    enable_reverse_proxy_auth: Boolean = false                  -- ENABLE_REVERSE_PROXY_AUTHENTICATION
    enable_reverse_proxy_auth_api: Boolean = false              -- ENABLE_REVERSE_PROXY_AUTHENTICATION_API
    enable_reverse_proxy_auto_registration: Boolean = false     -- ENABLE_REVERSE_PROXY_AUTO_REGISTRATION
    enable_reverse_proxy_email: Boolean = false                 -- ENABLE_REVERSE_PROXY_EMAIL
    enable_reverse_proxy_full_name: Boolean = false             -- ENABLE_REVERSE_PROXY_FULL_NAME
    enable_openid_signin: Boolean = false                       -- ENABLE_OPENID_SIGNIN (default true only before install)
    enable_openid_signup: Boolean = false                       -- ENABLE_OPENID_SIGNUP
    openid_allowed_uris: Set<String> = {}                       -- [openid] WHITELISTED_URIS (regexes)
    openid_blocked_uris: Set<String> = {}                       -- [openid] BLACKLISTED_URIS (regexes)

    -- [security]
    login_remember_days: Duration = 31.days                     -- LOGIN_REMEMBER_DAYS
    min_password_length: Integer = 8                            -- MIN_PASSWORD_LENGTH
    password_complexity: Set<PasswordCharacterClass> = {}       -- PASSWORD_COMPLEXITY (default "off")
    password_check_pwned: Boolean = false                       -- PASSWORD_CHECK_PWN (HaveIBeenPwned k-anonymity)
    global_two_factor_requirement: TwoFactorRequirement = none  -- GLOBAL_TWO_FACTOR_REQUIREMENT
    reverse_proxy_user_header: String = "X-WEBAUTH-USER"        -- REVERSE_PROXY_AUTHENTICATION_USER
    reverse_proxy_email_header: String = "X-WEBAUTH-EMAIL"      -- REVERSE_PROXY_AUTHENTICATION_EMAIL
    reverse_proxy_full_name_header: String = "X-WEBAUTH-FULLNAME" -- REVERSE_PROXY_AUTHENTICATION_FULL_NAME
    reverse_proxy_trusted_proxies: Set<String> = {"127.0.0.0/8", "::1/128"} -- REVERSE_PROXY_TRUSTED_PROXIES
    disable_query_auth_token: Boolean = false                   -- DISABLE_QUERY_AUTH_TOKEN

    -- [session]
    session_lifetime: Duration = 86400.seconds                  -- SESSION_LIFE_TIME
    session_gc_interval: Duration = 86400.seconds               -- GC_INTERVAL_TIME

    -- [admin] USER_DISABLED_FEATURES / EXTERNAL_USER_DISABLE_FEATURES live in accounts'
    -- config; the manage_password feature is read as
    -- user.has_feature_disabled(manage_password).

    -- [oauth2] provider
    oauth2_enabled: Boolean = true                              -- ENABLED
    oauth2_access_token_lifetime: Duration = 3600.seconds       -- ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRATION_TIME
    oauth2_refresh_token_lifetime: Duration = 730.hours         -- REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRATION_TIME
    oauth2_invalidate_refresh_tokens: Boolean = true            -- INVALIDATE_REFRESH_TOKENS
    oauth2_default_applications: Set<BuiltinOAuth2App> = {git_credential_oauth, git_credential_manager, tea} -- DEFAULT_APPLICATIONS
    oauth2_additional_grant_scopes: Boolean = false             -- ENABLE_ADDITIONAL_GRANT_SCOPES (groups claim honours public-only membership)
    oauth2_authorization_code_lifetime: Duration = 10.minutes   -- decided (new setting): 10 minutes, configurable; codes are single-use

    -- [oauth2_client] behaviour when the forge is an OAuth2 client
    oauth2_client_register_email_confirm: Boolean = false       -- REGISTER_EMAIL_CONFIRM (default = [service] value)
    oauth2_client_auto_registration: Boolean = false            -- ENABLE_AUTO_REGISTRATION
    oauth2_client_username_source: ExternalUsernameSource = nickname -- USERNAME
    oauth2_client_update_avatar: Boolean = false                -- UPDATE_AVATAR
    oauth2_client_account_linking: AccountLinkingMode = login   -- ACCOUNT_LINKING
    oauth2_client_openid_connect_scopes: Set<String> = {}       -- OPENID_CONNECT_SCOPES

    -- [authorized_integration]
    integration_allowed_domains: Set<String> = {}               -- ALLOWED_DOMAINS
    integration_blocked_domains: Set<String> = {}               -- BLOCKED_DOMAINS
    integration_allow_local_networks: Boolean = false           -- ALLOW_LOCALNETWORKS
    integration_request_timeout: Duration = 10.seconds          -- REQUEST_TIMEOUT
    integration_cache_ttl: Duration = 10.minutes                -- CACHE_TTL

    -- [cron.sync_external_users] UPDATE_EXISTING; the schedule is administration's
    -- CronTask sync_external_users (one schedule, kept there).
    -- The same setting as administration's config.sync_external_users_update_existing
    -- (one [cron.sync_external_users] UPDATE_EXISTING), used by the dashboard button.
    sync_external_users_update_existing: Boolean = true

    -- [ssh]
    ssh_trusted_user_ca_keys_configured: Boolean = false        -- TRUSTED_USER_CA_KEYS (HTTP-signature certificates)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: registration
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Open self-registration with a local password.
-- from: routers/web/auth/auth.go:484
rule VisitorRegisters {
    when: VisitorRegisters(session, name, email, password)
    requires: not (exists accounts/ReservedName{name: name})   -- accounts: a reserved name is refused until an admin releases it
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: not config.disable_registration
    requires: not config.allow_only_external_registration
    requires: config.enable_captcha = false or captcha_solved(session)
    requires: email_domain_allowed(email)
    requires: password_acceptable(password)
    requires: username_available(name)
    requires: email_available(email)

    let first_user = user_count() = 0
    let needs_confirmation = (config.register_email_confirm or config.register_manual_confirm) and first_user = false

    ensures:
        let user = accounts/User.created(
            name: name,
            primary_email: email,
            kind: individual,
            is_active: needs_confirmation = false,
            is_admin: first_user,
            is_restricted: config.default_user_is_restricted,
            prohibit_login: false
        )
        UserLogin.created(user: user, source: null, login_name: name, has_password: true, must_change_password: false, password_changed_at: now, last_sign_in_at: now)
        UserSignedUp(user)
        if needs_confirmation and config.register_email_confirm:
            EmailVerificationCode.created(user: user, purpose: user_activation, email: email, expires_at: now + config.activation_code_lifetime, status: pending)
            MailSendThrottle.created(user: user, kind: resend, until: now + config.mail_resend_interval)
        if needs_confirmation = false:
            session.status = authenticated
            session.user = user
            session.authenticated_via = password_login
            session.last_activity_at = now
            UserSignedIn(user: user, method: password_login)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/sign_up. Field limits: username max 40, e-mail max 254,
        -- password max 255. The first account ever created becomes an active site admin.
        -- With manual confirmation the new user sees "an administrator must activate
        -- your account" and nothing is mailed. The password must be typed twice.
}

-- An inactive, signed-in user asks for the activation mail again.
-- from: routers/web/auth/auth.go:697
rule InactiveUserRequestsActivationMail {
    when: InactiveUserRequestsActivationMail(user)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: not user.is_active
    requires: config.register_email_confirm
    requires: not exists MailSendThrottle{user: user, kind: resend}

    ensures:
        EmailVerificationCode.created(user: user, purpose: user_activation, email: user.primary_email, expires_at: now + config.activation_code_lifetime, status: pending)
        MailSendThrottle.created(user: user, kind: resend, until: now + config.mail_resend_interval)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /user/activate (no code). While throttled the page says "already sent,
        -- wait 3 minutes" and nothing is mailed.
}

-- An inactive user fixes a mistyped address before activating.
-- from: routers/web/auth/auth.go:767
rule InactiveUserReplacesUnconfirmedEmail {
    when: InactiveUserReplacesUnconfirmedEmail(user, email)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: not user.is_active
    requires: config.register_email_confirm
    requires: not exists MailSendThrottle{user: user, kind: email_change}
    requires: email_domain_allowed(email)
    requires: email_available(email)

    ensures:
        for c in EmailVerificationCodes where user = user and status = pending:
            c.status = revoked
    ensures: UnconfirmedPrimaryEmailReplaced(user: user, new_address: email)
    ensures: MailSendThrottle.created(user: user, kind: email_change, until: now + config.mail_resend_interval)
    ensures:
        EmailVerificationCode.created(user: user, purpose: user_activation, email: email, expires_at: now + config.activation_code_lifetime, status: pending)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/activate with `email`. The confirmation mail to the new address
        -- is sent on the follow-up page even if the resend throttle would otherwise apply.
}

-- Following the activation link. Local accounts must also re-enter their password, so
-- a leaked link alone cannot take over the account.
-- from: routers/web/auth/auth.go:767
rule UserActivatesAccount {
    when: UserActivatesAccount(session, code, password)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: code.purpose = user_activation
    requires: code.is_valid
    let login = UserLogin{user: code.user}
    requires: login.is_local = false or password_matches(code.user, password)
    requires: not code.user.being_purged         -- accounts: a purge disabled the account; a stale link must not revive it

    ensures: code.status = used
    ensures: code.user.is_active = true
    ensures: EmailConfirmationLinkFollowed(user: code.user, email: code.email)
    ensures: AccountActivated(user: code.user)
    ensures: login.last_sign_in_at = now
    ensures:
        if session.status = anonymous:
            session.status = authenticated
            session.user = code.user
            session.authenticated_via = activation
            session.last_activity_at = now

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /user/activate?code=… then POST with the password. An unknown,
        -- expired or already-used code shows "invalid or expired". Activation regenerates
        -- the session and signs the user in.
}

-- Confirming an additional (non-primary) e-mail address.
-- from: routers/web/auth/auth.go:897
rule UserConfirmsEmailAddress {
    when: UserConfirmsEmailAddress(code, email)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: code.purpose = email_activation
    requires: code.is_valid
    requires: code.email = email

    ensures: code.status = used
    ensures: EmailConfirmationLinkFollowed(user: code.user, email: email)
    ensures:
        for t in MailSendThrottles where user = code.user and kind = resend:
            not exists t

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/activate_email?code=…&email=…. Does not require being
        -- signed in and does not sign anyone in.
}

-- accounts asks for an additional address to be confirmed.
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:71
rule IssueEmailConfirmationCode {
    when: accounts/UserEmailAdded(user, address)

    requires: config.register_email_confirm

    ensures:
        EmailVerificationCode.created(user: user, purpose: email_activation, email: address, expires_at: now + config.activation_code_lifetime, status: pending)
}

-- accounts asks for the confirmation mail to be sent again.
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:71
rule ReissueEmailConfirmationCode {
    when: accounts/EmailActivationRequested(user, address)

    ensures:
        for c in EmailVerificationCodes where user = user and purpose = email_activation and status = pending:
            c.status = revoked
    ensures: EmailVerificationCode.created(user: user, purpose: email_activation, email: address, expires_at: now + config.activation_code_lifetime, status: pending)
}

-- Replacing the primary address kills every outstanding mailed code and remember-me.
-- from: services/user/email.go:176
rule PrimaryEmailChangeRevokesCodes {
    when: accounts/PrimaryEmailChanged(user, old_address, new_address)

    ensures:
        for c in EmailVerificationCodes where user = user and status = pending:
            c.status = revoked
    ensures:
        for t in LongTermAuthorizations where user = user and status = active:
            t.status = revoked
}

-- Every freshly issued code is mailed to the address it is for.
-- from: services/mailer/mail.go:39
rule VerificationCodeMailed {
    when: code: EmailVerificationCode.created
    ensures:
        if code.purpose = user_activation:
            ActivationEmailRequested(user: code.user, code: code)
        if code.purpose = password_reset:
            PasswordResetRequested(user: code.user, code: code)
        if code.purpose = email_activation:
            EmailConfirmationRequested(user: code.user, email: code.email, code: code)
}

-- from: models/user/user.go:973
rule VerificationCodeExpires {
    when: mailed: EmailVerificationCode.expires_at <= now
    requires: mailed.status = pending
    ensures: mailed.status = expired
}

rule MailThrottleLapses {
    when: throttle: MailSendThrottle.until <= now
    ensures: not exists throttle
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: interactive sign-in
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Password sign-in. The login may be the username or an activated e-mail address; the
-- password is checked by the user's UserLogin source (local store, LDAP, SMTP, PAM).
-- Unknown logins are tried against every active password source, which may
-- auto-provision the account (see ExternalPasswordSourceProvisionsUser).
-- decided: an unconfirmed (inactive) account is not refused here; it gets the limited
-- session Forgejo gives it, which can only resend activation or sign out
-- (UserLogin.may_use_account, surface AccountActivation).
-- from: routers/web/auth/auth.go:214
rule VisitorSignsInWithPassword {
    when: VisitorSignsInWithPassword(session, user, password, remember)

    let login = UserLogin{user: user}

    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: config.enable_internal_signin
    requires: config.enable_captcha = false or config.require_captcha_for_login = false or captcha_solved(session)
    requires: exists login
    requires: login.source = null or login.source.is_active
    requires: password_matches(user, password)
    requires: not user.prohibit_login
    requires: not user.being_purged             -- accounts: a purge in progress refuses sign-in
    requires: user.kind = individual

    let needs_second_factor = login.has_second_factor and not login.skips_local_two_factor

    -- An LDAP bind refreshes what the directory says about the account on every
    -- sign-in, before any second factor: its groups (team and quota-group
    -- mapping, decided: quota 8) and its SSH keys.
    -- from: services/auth/source/ldap/source_authenticate.go:30
    ensures:
        if login.source != null and login.source.is_ldap and login.source.settings.groups_enabled:
            ExternalGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: login.source, groups: DirectoryEntry{source: login.source, username: login.login_name}.groups)
            ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: login.source, groups: DirectoryEntry{source: login.source, username: login.login_name}.groups)
    ensures:
        if login.source != null and login.source.is_ldap:
            ExternalSshKeysAsserted(user: user, source: login.source, keys: DirectoryEntry{source: login.source, username: login.login_name}.ssh_public_keys)
    ensures:
        if needs_second_factor:
            session.status = pending_second_factor
            session.pending_user = user
            session.remember_requested = remember
        else:
            session.status = authenticated
            session.user = user
            session.authenticated_via = password_login
            session.last_activity_at = now
            login.last_sign_in_at = now
            UserSignedIn(user: user, method: password_login)
            if remember:
                let lta = LongTermAuthorization.created(user: user, sso_source: null, expires_at: now + config.login_remember_days, status: active)
                session.remember_me = lta

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/login (form max: login 254, password 255). Failures all say
        -- "username or password is incorrect"; a prohibited account sees the "sign-in
        -- prohibited" page. Inactive accounts DO get a session — every page then shows
        -- the activation page (see UserLogin.may_use_account). When the instance has
        -- internal sign-in disabled and exactly one OAuth2 source, the login page
        -- redirects straight to that provider. With WebAuthn enrolled the second-factor
        -- page offers the security key first, falling back to TOTP. A passkey skips this
        -- form altogether (VisitorSignsInWithPasskey).
}

-- An LDAP/SMTP/PAM bind succeeds for a login no local account has yet.
-- from: services/auth/source/ldap/source_authenticate.go:30
rule ExternalPasswordSourceProvisionsUser {
    when: VisitorSignsInWithExternalPassword(session, source, entry, password)
    requires: not (exists accounts/ReservedName{name: entry.username})   -- accounts: a reserved name is refused until an admin releases it
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: config.enable_internal_signin
    requires: source.is_active
    requires: source.verifies_passwords
    requires: entry.source = source
    requires: source_accepts_password(source, entry, password)
    requires: username_available(entry.username)

    ensures:
        let user = accounts/User.created(
            name: entry.username,
            primary_email: entry.email,
            kind: individual,
            is_active: true,
            is_admin: entry.is_admin,
            is_restricted: entry.is_restricted,
            prohibit_login: false
        )
        UserLogin.created(user: user, source: source, login_name: entry.username, has_password: false, must_change_password: false, password_changed_at: null, last_sign_in_at: now)
        UserSignedUp(user)
        ExternalSshKeysAsserted(user: user, source: source, keys: entry.ssh_public_keys)
        ExternalGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: source, groups: entry.groups)
        ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: source, groups: entry.groups)
        session.status = authenticated
        session.user = user
        session.authenticated_via = password_login
        session.last_activity_at = now
        UserSignedIn(user: user, method: password_login)

    @guidance
        -- LDAP: e-mail defaults to <username>@localhost.local when the directory has none;
        -- admin/restricted come from the admin/restricted filters. SMTP: the login must be
        -- an address in an allowed domain; name = lower-cased local part. PAM: e-mail =
        -- login@pam_email_domain. On every later successful bind LDAP refreshes
        -- admin/restricted flags, SSH keys and group→team mapping.
}

-- Second factor: TOTP passcode. A passcode that was already used is refused.
-- from: routers/web/auth/2fa.go:43
rule VisitorCompletesTotpChallenge {
    when: VisitorCompletesTotpChallenge(session, passcode)

    requires: session.status = pending_second_factor
    let user = session.pending_user
    requires: not user.being_purged              -- a purge may have started since the first factor
    let twofa = TwoFactor{user: user}
    requires: exists twofa
    requires: totp_valid(twofa, passcode)
    requires: twofa.last_used_passcode != passcode

    ensures: twofa.last_used_passcode = passcode
    ensures: session.status = authenticated
    ensures: session.user = user
    ensures: session.pending_user = null
    ensures: session.authenticated_via = totp
    ensures: session.last_activity_at = now
    ensures: UserLogin{user: user}.last_sign_in_at = now
    ensures: UserSignedIn(user: user, method: totp)
    ensures:
        if session.pending_link and session.pending_external_identity != null:
            ExternalLogin.created(user: user, source: session.pending_external_identity.source, external_id: session.pending_external_identity.external_id, provider: session.pending_external_identity.source.settings.provider, email: session.pending_external_identity.email, name: session.pending_external_identity.full_name, nickname: session.pending_external_identity.nickname, avatar_url: session.pending_external_identity.avatar_url, linked_at: now)
        if session.pending_openid_uri != null:
            OpenIDIdentity.created(user: user, uri: session.pending_openid_uri, show_publicly: false)
        if session.remember_requested:
            let lta = LongTermAuthorization.created(user: user, sso_source: session.pending_sso_source, expires_at: now + config.login_remember_days, status: active)
            session.remember_me = lta

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/two_factor.
}

-- Second factor: the scratch (recovery) code. It works once and is replaced; the user
-- lands on the security settings page to note the new one.
-- from: routers/web/auth/2fa.go:123
rule VisitorUsesScratchCode {
    when: VisitorUsesScratchCode(session, scratch_code)

    requires: session.status = pending_second_factor
    let user = session.pending_user
    requires: not user.being_purged              -- a purge may have started since the first factor
    let twofa = TwoFactor{user: user}
    requires: exists twofa
    requires: scratch_code_valid(twofa, scratch_code)

    ensures: twofa.scratch_code_generation = twofa.scratch_code_generation + 1
    ensures: session.status = authenticated
    ensures: session.user = user
    ensures: session.pending_user = null
    ensures: session.authenticated_via = scratch_code
    ensures: session.last_activity_at = now
    ensures: UserSignedIn(user: user, method: scratch_code)
    ensures:
        if session.pending_openid_uri != null:
            OpenIDIdentity.created(user: user, uri: session.pending_openid_uri, show_publicly: false)
        if session.remember_requested:
            let lta = LongTermAuthorization.created(user: user, sso_source: session.pending_sso_source, expires_at: now + config.login_remember_days, status: active)
            session.remember_me = lta

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/two_factor/scratch.
}

-- Second factor: a WebAuthn assertion. A signature counter that went backwards means
-- a cloned authenticator and the assertion is refused.
-- from: routers/web/auth/webauthn.go:89
rule VisitorCompletesWebAuthnChallenge {
    when: VisitorCompletesWebAuthnChallenge(session, credential, sign_count)

    requires: session.status = pending_second_factor
    let user = session.pending_user
    requires: not user.being_purged              -- a purge may have started since the first factor
    requires: credential.user = user
    requires: webauthn_assertion_valid(credential)
    requires: sign_count > credential.sign_count or (sign_count = 0 and credential.sign_count = 0)

    ensures: credential.sign_count = sign_count
    ensures: session.status = authenticated
    ensures: session.user = user
    ensures: session.pending_user = null
    ensures: session.authenticated_via = webauthn
    ensures: session.last_activity_at = now
    ensures: UserSignedIn(user: user, method: webauthn)
    ensures:
        if session.pending_link and session.pending_external_identity != null:
            ExternalLogin.created(user: user, source: session.pending_external_identity.source, external_id: session.pending_external_identity.external_id, provider: session.pending_external_identity.source.settings.provider, email: session.pending_external_identity.email, name: session.pending_external_identity.full_name, nickname: session.pending_external_identity.nickname, avatar_url: session.pending_external_identity.avatar_url, linked_at: now)
        if session.pending_openid_uri != null:
            OpenIDIdentity.created(user: user, uri: session.pending_openid_uri, show_publicly: false)
        if session.remember_requested:
            let lta = LongTermAuthorization.created(user: user, sso_source: session.pending_sso_source, expires_at: now + config.login_remember_days, status: active)
            session.remember_me = lta

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /user/webauthn, GET/POST /user/webauthn/assertion. Any credential,
        -- passkey or not, works here as the second factor. Legacy credentials get their
        -- backup flags filled in on first use.
}

-- Passwordless sign-in with a passkey: the discoverable credential names its user and,
-- with user verification, stands for both factors, so no second-factor step follows.
-- decided: passkey passwordless sign-in is part of the rebuild; security keys that are
-- not discoverable remain second factors only.
-- from: routers/web/auth/webauthn.go:89 (assertion check and counter rule reused)
rule VisitorSignsInWithPasskey {
    when: VisitorSignsInWithPasskey(session, credential, sign_count, remember)

    let user = credential.user
    let login = UserLogin{user: user}

    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: config.enable_internal_signin
    requires: credential.discoverable
    requires: webauthn_assertion_valid(credential)
    requires: sign_count > credential.sign_count or (sign_count = 0 and credential.sign_count = 0)
    requires: exists login
    requires: login.source = null or login.source.is_active
    requires: not user.prohibit_login
    requires: not user.being_purged
    requires: user.kind = individual

    ensures: credential.sign_count = sign_count
    ensures: session.status = authenticated
    ensures: session.user = user
    ensures: session.authenticated_via = passkey
    ensures: session.last_activity_at = now
    ensures: login.last_sign_in_at = now
    ensures: UserSignedIn(user: user, method: passkey)
    ensures:
        if remember:
            let lta = LongTermAuthorization.created(user: user, sso_source: null, expires_at: now + config.login_remember_days, status: active)
            session.remember_me = lta

    @guidance
        -- Web: "sign in with a passkey" on /user/login runs a WebAuthn assertion with an
        -- empty allow-list and user verification required; the authenticator picks the
        -- credential. A non-discoverable security key cannot be used this way.
}

-- The remember-me cookie re-establishes a session.
-- from: routers/web/auth/auth.go:53
rule VisitorResumesWithRememberMe {
    when: VisitorResumesWithRememberMe(session, lta)

    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: lta.status = active
    requires: not lta.is_sso
    requires: not lta.user.being_purged

    ensures: session.status = authenticated
    ensures: session.user = lta.user
    ensures: session.remember_me = lta
    ensures: session.authenticated_via = remember_me
    ensures: session.last_activity_at = now
    ensures: UserSignedIn(user: lta.user, method: remember_me)

    @guidance
        -- Any page visited without a session but with the remember cookie bounces via
        -- /user/login, which performs this. An unknown or mismatching cookie is deleted.
}

-- The SSO-bound remember-me cookie is spent on a silent re-authentication at the IdP.
-- from: routers/web/auth/auth.go:84
rule VisitorResumesWithSsoRememberMe {
    when: VisitorResumesWithRememberMe(session, lta)

    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: lta.status = active
    requires: lta.is_sso
    requires: lta.sso_source.is_active
    requires: lta.sso_source.kind = oauth2

    ensures: lta.status = consumed
    ensures: OAuth2ProviderRedirectRequested(session: session, source: lta.sso_source, prompt_none: true)

    @guidance
        -- Redirects to /user/oauth2/{source}?prompt=none. If the IdP answers
        -- login_required / interaction_required / consent_required /
        -- account_selection_required, the browser is sent through the normal
        -- interactive provider sign-in instead.
}

-- from: models/user/user.go:973
rule LongTermAuthorizationExpires {
    when: lta: LongTermAuthorization.expires_at <= now
    requires: lta.status = active
    ensures: lta.status = expired
}

-- Any browser request without a session cookie starts an anonymous session.
-- from: models/auth/session.go:36
rule VisitorArrives {
    when: VisitorArrives()
    ensures: Session.created(status: anonymous, user: null, authenticated_via: null, pending_user: null, remember_requested: false, pending_sso_source: null, pending_external_identity: null, pending_link: false, pending_openid_uri: null, remember_me: null, last_activity_at: now)
}

-- decided: signing out revokes this device's remember-me record server-side (Forgejo
-- only deleted the cookie); other devices stay remembered.
-- from: routers/web/auth/auth.go:434
rule UserSignsOut {
    when: UserSignsOut(session)

    requires: session.status = authenticated

    ensures: session.status = destroyed
    ensures:
        if session.remember_me != null and session.remember_me.status = active:
            session.remember_me.status = revoked
    ensures: UserSignedOut(user: session.user, session: session)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/logout. Clears the session and the remember-me and redirect
        -- cookies, revokes the remember-me record the cookie named, and tells the
        -- user's other open tabs via the event stream.
}

-- from: models/auth/session.go:113
rule SessionExpires {
    when: session: Session.last_activity_at + config.session_lifetime <= now
    requires: session.status in {anonymous, pending_second_factor, authenticated}
    ensures: session.status = destroyed
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: external identity providers (forge as OAuth2/OIDC client)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:955
rule VisitorStartsProviderSignIn {
    when: VisitorStartsProviderSignIn(session, source, prompt_none)

    requires: source.kind = oauth2
    requires: source.is_active

    ensures: OAuth2ProviderRedirectRequested(session, source, prompt_none)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /user/oauth2/{source-name}. PKCE (S256) is used towards providers that
        -- support it (OpenID Connect and a few others). `redirect_to` is remembered across
        -- the round-trip.
}

-- The provider came back with an identity that maps to an existing account (by the
-- account's login name at this source, or by an ExternalLogin link).
-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:1355
rule ProviderReturnsKnownIdentity {
    when: ProviderReturnsIdentity(session, identity)

    let source = identity.source
    let known_login = UserLogin{source: source, login_name: identity.external_id}
    let known_link = ExternalLogin{source: source, external_id: identity.external_id}
    let user = if exists known_login: known_login.user else: known_link.user

    requires: source.is_active
    requires: source.settings.required_claim_name = null or claim_satisfied(identity, source.settings.required_claim_name, source.settings.required_claim_value)
    requires: exists known_login or exists known_link
    requires: not user.prohibit_login
    requires: not user.being_purged

    let needs_second_factor = not source.settings.skip_local_two_factor and UserLogin{user: user}.has_second_factor

    ensures: ExternalAvatarAsserted(user: user, url: identity.avatar_url)
    ensures: ExternalSshKeysAsserted(user: user, source: source, keys: identity.ssh_public_keys)
    ensures: ExternalGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: source, groups: identity.groups)
    ensures: ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: source, groups: identity.quota_groups)
    ensures: ExternalAdminFlagsAsserted(user: user, is_admin: admin_from_groups(source, identity), is_restricted: restricted_from_groups(source, identity, user.is_restricted))
    ensures:
        if exists known_link:
            known_link.email = identity.email
            known_link.nickname = identity.nickname
            known_link.avatar_url = identity.avatar_url
    ensures:
        if needs_second_factor:
            session.status = pending_second_factor
            session.pending_user = user
            session.remember_requested = true
            session.pending_sso_source = source
        else:
            session.status = authenticated
            session.user = user
            session.authenticated_via = external_provider
            session.last_activity_at = now
            UserSignedIn(user: user, method: external_provider)
            let lta = LongTermAuthorization.created(user: user, sso_source: source, expires_at: now + config.login_remember_days, status: active)
            session.remember_me = lta

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /user/oauth2/{source-name}/callback. Provider errors access_denied /
        -- temporarily_unavailable are shown as a flash on the login page. A missing
        -- required claim is treated as "sign-in prohibited". Signing in through a
        -- provider always issues the SSO-bound remember-me.
}

-- A signed-in user came back from a provider: link that identity to their account.
-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:1096
rule ProviderIdentityLinkedToSignedInUser {
    when: ProviderReturnsIdentity(session, identity)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    let source = identity.source
    requires: source.is_active
    requires: session.status = authenticated
    requires: not exists UserLogin{source: source, login_name: identity.external_id}
    requires: not exists ExternalLogin{source: source, external_id: identity.external_id}

    ensures: ExternalLogin.created(user: session.user, source: source, external_id: identity.external_id, provider: source.settings.provider, email: identity.email, name: identity.full_name, nickname: identity.nickname, avatar_url: identity.avatar_url, linked_at: now)

    @guidance
        -- Lands on /user/settings/security. Linking also re-attributes migrated issues and
        -- comments whose original author had this external id on a supported forge.
}

-- Unknown identity, nobody signed in, auto-registration on: create the account.
-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:1104
-- A person signing in through an OAuth2 source for the first time may be the
-- original author of migrated content: a remote placeholder account (kind
-- `remote`) whose remote source matches this OAuth2 source and whose login name
-- is this external id. accounts promotes that placeholder to a real account.
-- from: services/remote/promote.go:52
rule ProviderIdentityClaimsRemotePlaceholder {
    when: ProviderReturnsIdentity(session, identity)
    let source = identity.source
    let placeholder = remote_placeholder_for(source, identity.external_id)
    requires: source.is_active
    requires: placeholder != null
    requires: identity.email != null
    ensures: RemoteUserClaimed(user: placeholder, email: identity.email)
    @guidance
        -- remote_placeholder_for: the accounts/User of kind remote whose sign-in
        -- source is a Remote source matching `source` (same provider URL) and whose
        -- login name equals the external id; null when there is none.
}

rule ProviderIdentityAutoRegisters {
    when: ProviderReturnsIdentity(session, identity)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    let source = identity.source
    let name = external_username(identity, config.oauth2_client_username_source)
    requires: source.is_active
    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: not exists UserLogin{source: source, login_name: identity.external_id}
    requires: not exists ExternalLogin{source: source, external_id: identity.external_id}
    requires: config.oauth2_client_auto_registration
    requires: not config.allow_only_internal_registration
    requires: identity.email != null
    requires: name != null
    requires: username_available(name)
    requires: not (exists accounts/ReservedName{name: name})   -- accounts: a reserved name is refused until an admin releases it
    requires: email_available(identity.email)

    let needs_confirmation = config.oauth2_client_register_email_confirm or config.register_manual_confirm

    ensures:
        let user = accounts/User.created(
            name: name,
            primary_email: identity.email,
            kind: individual,
            is_active: not needs_confirmation,
            is_admin: admin_from_groups(source, identity),
            is_restricted: restricted_from_groups(source, identity, config.default_user_is_restricted),
            prohibit_login: false
        )
        UserLogin.created(user: user, source: source, login_name: identity.external_id, has_password: false, must_change_password: false, password_changed_at: null, last_sign_in_at: now)
        UserSignedUp(user)
        ExternalGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: source, groups: identity.groups)
        ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: source, groups: identity.quota_groups)
        if needs_confirmation and config.oauth2_client_register_email_confirm:
            EmailVerificationCode.created(user: user, purpose: user_activation, email: identity.email, expires_at: now + config.activation_code_lifetime, status: pending)
        session.status = authenticated
        session.user = user
        session.authenticated_via = external_provider
        session.last_activity_at = now
        UserSignedIn(user: user, method: external_provider)

    @guidance
        -- The username is taken from the configured claim (userid, nickname, the local
        -- part of the e-mail, or preferred_username) and normalised. If the provider did
        -- not supply the e-mail or the chosen username claim, the visitor is sent to the
        -- link-account page instead (ProviderIdentityNeedsLinking). If the name or e-mail
        -- collides with an existing account, account_linking decides: `auto` links to
        -- that account (ProviderIdentityAutoLinksExistingAccount), `login` asks the
        -- visitor to sign in to it, `disabled` fails.
}

-- E-mail collision with account_linking = auto: link silently, but only to the account
-- holding that e-mail and only when the IdP vouches for the address.
-- decided: auto-link matches by e-mail only and requires the IdP's email_verified claim;
-- otherwise the visitor must sign in to the local account to link it
-- (ProviderIdentityNeedsLinking).
-- from: routers/web/auth/auth.go:581
rule ProviderIdentityAutoLinksExistingAccount {
    when: ProviderReturnsIdentity(session, identity)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    let source = identity.source
    let existing = user_by_email(identity.email)
    requires: source.is_active
    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: not exists UserLogin{source: source, login_name: identity.external_id}
    requires: not exists ExternalLogin{source: source, external_id: identity.external_id}
    requires: config.oauth2_client_auto_registration
    requires: config.oauth2_client_account_linking = auto
    requires: identity.email != null
    requires: identity.email_verified
    requires: existing != null
    requires: not existing.being_purged
    requires: not UserLogin{user: existing}.has_second_factor

    ensures: ExternalLogin.created(user: existing, source: source, external_id: identity.external_id, provider: source.settings.provider, email: identity.email, name: identity.full_name, nickname: identity.nickname, avatar_url: identity.avatar_url, linked_at: now)
    ensures: session.status = authenticated
    ensures: session.user = existing
    ensures: session.authenticated_via = external_provider
    ensures: session.last_activity_at = now
    ensures: UserSignedIn(user: existing, method: external_provider)
}

-- Unknown identity and no auto-registration (or missing fields, or a collision with an
-- existing account that may not be linked automatically): park it in the session and
-- offer "link to an existing account" / "register".
-- decided: an e-mail the IdP has not verified never auto-links; the collision lands here.
-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:1278
rule ProviderIdentityNeedsLinking {
    when: ProviderReturnsIdentity(session, identity)

    let source = identity.source
    let name = external_username(identity, config.oauth2_client_username_source)
    let existing = user_by_email(identity.email)
    let collides = (identity.email != null and not email_available(identity.email)) or (name != null and not username_available(name))
    let auto_linkable = config.oauth2_client_account_linking = auto and identity.email_verified and existing != null and not UserLogin{user: existing}.has_second_factor
    requires: source.is_active
    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: not exists UserLogin{source: source, login_name: identity.external_id}
    requires: not exists ExternalLogin{source: source, external_id: identity.external_id}
    requires: not config.oauth2_client_auto_registration or config.allow_only_internal_registration or identity.email = null or name = null or (collides and config.oauth2_client_account_linking != disabled and not auto_linkable)

    ensures: session.pending_external_identity = identity

    @guidance
        -- Web: redirect to GET /user/link_account (only reachable when OpenID or OAuth2 is
        -- enabled). The page pre-fills the username/e-mail and says when an account with
        -- that e-mail or name already exists.
}

-- Link the pending identity by proving ownership of an existing account.
-- from: routers/web/auth/linkaccount.go:102
rule VisitorLinksPendingIdentityBySignIn {
    when: VisitorLinksPendingIdentityBySignIn(session, user, password, remember)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: session.pending_external_identity != null
    requires: config.enable_captcha = false or config.require_external_registration_captcha = false or captcha_solved(session)
    requires: password_matches(user, password)
    requires: not user.prohibit_login
    requires: not user.being_purged

    let identity = session.pending_external_identity
    let needs_second_factor = UserLogin{user: user}.has_second_factor

    ensures:
        if needs_second_factor:
            session.status = pending_second_factor
            session.pending_user = user
            session.remember_requested = remember
            session.pending_link = true
        else:
            ExternalLogin.created(user: user, source: identity.source, external_id: identity.external_id, provider: identity.source.settings.provider, email: identity.email, name: identity.full_name, nickname: identity.nickname, avatar_url: identity.avatar_url, linked_at: now)
            session.status = authenticated
            session.user = user
            session.authenticated_via = password_login
            session.last_activity_at = now
            UserSignedIn(user: user, method: password_login)
            ExternalGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: identity.source, groups: identity.groups)
            ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: identity.source, groups: identity.quota_groups)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/link_account_signin. With 2FA enrolled the link is made after
        -- the second factor succeeds.
}

-- Register a new account for the pending identity.
-- from: routers/web/auth/linkaccount.go:182
rule VisitorRegistersFromPendingIdentity {
    when: VisitorRegistersFromPendingIdentity(session, name, email, password)
    requires: not (exists accounts/ReservedName{name: name})   -- accounts: a reserved name is refused until an admin releases it
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: session.pending_external_identity != null
    requires: not config.disable_registration
    requires: not config.allow_only_internal_registration
    requires: config.enable_captcha = false or config.require_external_registration_captcha = false or captcha_solved(session)
    requires: email_domain_allowed(email)
    requires: password = null or password_acceptable(password)
    requires: username_available(name)
    requires: email_available(email)

    let identity = session.pending_external_identity
    let keeps_password = config.require_external_registration_password and not config.allow_only_external_registration and password != null

    ensures:
        let user = accounts/User.created(
            name: name,
            primary_email: email,
            kind: individual,
            is_active: not (config.register_email_confirm or config.register_manual_confirm),
            is_admin: false,
            is_restricted: config.default_user_is_restricted,
            prohibit_login: false
        )
        UserLogin.created(user: user, source: identity.source, login_name: identity.external_id, has_password: keeps_password, must_change_password: false, password_changed_at: null, last_sign_in_at: now)
        ExternalLogin.created(user: user, source: identity.source, external_id: identity.external_id, provider: identity.source.settings.provider, email: identity.email, name: identity.full_name, nickname: identity.nickname, avatar_url: identity.avatar_url, linked_at: now)
        UserSignedUp(user)
        ExternalGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: identity.source, groups: identity.groups)
        ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: identity.source, groups: identity.quota_groups)
        session.pending_external_identity = null
        session.status = authenticated
        session.user = user
        session.authenticated_via = external_provider
        session.last_activity_at = now
        UserSignedIn(user: user, method: external_provider)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/link_account_signup. A password is only kept when
        -- REQUIRE_EXTERNAL_REGISTRATION_PASSWORD is on; otherwise the account has no local
        -- password (the user can still set one via "forgot password" if allowed).
}

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/security/security.go:42
rule UserUnlinksExternalLogin {
    when: UserUnlinksExternalLogin(user, link)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: link.user = user
    requires: config.oauth2_enabled or config.enable_openid_signin or config.enable_openid_signup

    ensures: not exists link

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/settings/security/account_link.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: OpenID 2.0 relying party
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: routers/web/auth/openid.go:127
rule VisitorSignsInWithOpenID {
    when: VisitorSignsInWithOpenID(session, uri)

    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: config.enable_openid_signin
    requires: openid_uri_allowed(uri)
    requires: openid_assertion_verified(uri)
    let identity = OpenIDIdentity{uri: uri}
    requires: not exists identity or not identity.user.being_purged

    ensures:
        if exists identity:
            if UserLogin{user: identity.user}.has_second_factor:
                session.status = pending_second_factor
                session.pending_user = identity.user
            else:
                session.status = authenticated
                session.user = identity.user
                session.authenticated_via = openid
                session.last_activity_at = now
                UserSignedIn(user: identity.user, method: openid)
        else:
            session.pending_openid_uri = uri

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/login/openid, then /user/openid/connect (attach to an
        -- existing account by signing in) or /user/openid/register (needs
        -- ENABLE_OPENID_SIGNUP). URIs must match an allow-list pattern when one is set
        -- and must not match a block-list pattern.
}

-- from: routers/web/auth/openid.go:256
rule VisitorConnectsOpenIDToAccount {
    when: VisitorConnectsOpenIDToAccount(session, user, password)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: session.status = anonymous
    requires: session.pending_openid_uri != null
    requires: password_matches(user, password)
    requires: not user.prohibit_login
    requires: not user.being_purged

    ensures:
        if UserLogin{user: user}.has_second_factor:
            session.status = pending_second_factor
            session.pending_user = user
        else:
            OpenIDIdentity.created(user: user, uri: session.pending_openid_uri, show_publicly: false)
            session.status = authenticated
            session.user = user
            session.authenticated_via = openid
            session.last_activity_at = now
            UserSignedIn(user: user, method: openid)
}

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/security/openid.go:22
rule UserAddsOpenID {
    when: UserAddsOpenID(user, uri)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: config.enable_openid_signin
    requires: openid_uri_allowed(uri)
    requires: openid_assertion_verified(uri)
    requires: not exists OpenIDIdentity{uri: uri}
    ensures: OpenIDIdentity.created(user: user, uri: uri, show_publicly: false)
}

-- from: models/user/openid.go:85
rule UserRemovesOpenID {
    when: UserRemovesOpenID(user, identity)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: identity.user = user
    ensures: not exists identity
}

-- from: models/user/openid.go:108
rule UserTogglesOpenIDVisibility {
    when: UserTogglesOpenIDVisibility(user, identity)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: identity.user = user
    ensures: identity.show_publicly = not identity.show_publicly
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: passwords
------------------------------------------------------------

-- "Forgot password". The answer is identical whether or not the address is known.
-- decided: the reset link lives for reset_code_lifetime, the lifetime the mail states
-- (Forgejo used the activation lifetime).
-- decided: the admin chooses the throttle: shared with activation resends (the default,
-- Forgejo's behaviour) or one of its own (mail_throttle_shared = false).
-- from: routers/web/auth/password.go:52
rule VisitorRequestsPasswordReset {
    when: VisitorRequestsPasswordReset(session, user)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    let login = UserLogin{user: user}
    requires: config.mail_service_configured
    requires: login.may_reset_password
    requires: (config.mail_throttle_shared and not exists MailSendThrottle{user: user, kind: resend}) or (not config.mail_throttle_shared and not exists MailSendThrottle{user: user, kind: password_reset})

    ensures:
        EmailVerificationCode.created(user: user, purpose: password_reset, email: user.primary_email, expires_at: now + config.reset_code_lifetime, status: pending)
        if config.mail_throttle_shared:
            MailSendThrottle.created(user: user, kind: resend, until: now + config.mail_resend_interval)
        else:
            MailSendThrottle.created(user: user, kind: password_reset, until: now + config.mail_resend_interval)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/forgot_password (hidden when no mailer is configured). The
        -- user is found by any of their e-mail addresses. Accounts whose password lives in
        -- LDAP/SMTP/PAM are told "this is not a local account".
}

-- Completing the reset. If TOTP is enrolled the user must also give a passcode or the
-- scratch code (which is then replaced). All remember-me tokens die with the old password.
-- from: routers/web/auth/password.go:177
rule VisitorResetsPassword {
    when: VisitorResetsPassword(session, code, new_password, passcode, scratch_code)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: code.purpose = password_reset
    requires: code.is_valid
    requires: session.user = null or session.user = code.user
    let user = code.user
    let login = UserLogin{user: user}
    let twofa = TwoFactor{user: user}
    requires: login.may_reset_password
    requires: not user.being_purged              -- accounts: no session for an account being purged
    requires: password_acceptable(new_password)
    requires: not exists twofa or (passcode != null and totp_valid(twofa, passcode) and twofa.last_used_passcode != passcode) or (scratch_code != null and scratch_code_valid(twofa, scratch_code))

    ensures: code.status = used
    ensures: login.has_password = true
    ensures: login.must_change_password = false
    ensures: login.password_changed_at = now
    ensures:
        for t in LongTermAuthorizations where user = user and status = active:
            t.status = revoked
    ensures: PasswordChanged(user)
    ensures:
        if exists twofa and scratch_code != null:
            twofa.scratch_code_generation = twofa.scratch_code_generation + 1
        if exists twofa and passcode != null:
            twofa.last_used_passcode = passcode
    ensures: session.status = authenticated
    ensures: session.user = user
    ensures: session.authenticated_via = password_reset
    ensures: session.last_activity_at = now
    ensures: UserSignedIn(user: user, method: password_reset)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/recover_account?code=…. The code is only consumed on POST,
        -- so merely opening the link does not burn it. A signed-in user opening someone
        -- else's code is told it belongs to another account.
}

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/account.go:48
rule UserChangesPassword {
    when: UserChangesPassword(user, old_password, new_password)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    let login = UserLogin{user: user}
    requires: not user.has_feature_disabled(manage_password)   -- accounts' USER_DISABLED_FEATURES / EXTERNAL_USER_DISABLE_FEATURES
    requires: login.is_local or login.source.kind = oauth2
    requires: login.has_password = false or password_matches(user, old_password)
    requires: password_acceptable(new_password)

    ensures: login.has_password = true
    ensures: login.must_change_password = false
    ensures: login.password_changed_at = now
    ensures:
        for t in LongTermAuthorizations where user = user and status = active:
            t.status = revoked
    ensures: PasswordChanged(user)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/settings/account. If the browser carried a remember-me cookie a
        -- fresh one is issued so this device stays remembered.
}

-- An admin-created account (or an admin reset) forces a new password before anything
-- else can be done.
-- from: routers/web/auth/password.go:278
rule UserChangesForcedPassword {
    when: UserChangesForcedPassword(user, new_password)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    let login = UserLogin{user: user}
    requires: login.must_change_password
    requires: password_acceptable(new_password)

    ensures: login.has_password = true
    ensures: login.must_change_password = false
    ensures: login.password_changed_at = now
    ensures:
        for t in LongTermAuthorizations where user = user and status = active:
            t.status = revoked
    ensures: PasswordChanged(user)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/settings/change_password. Every other page redirects here
        -- while the flag is set; git clients get 401 "must change password"; the API
        -- answers 403.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: second factors (settings)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/security/2fa.go:205
rule UserEnrolsTotp {
    when: UserEnrolsTotp(user, passcode)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: not exists TwoFactor{user: user}
    requires: enrolment_passcode_valid(user, passcode)

    ensures: TwoFactor.created(user: user, last_used_passcode: null, scratch_code_generation: 1, enrolled_at: now)
    ensures: TotpEnrolled(user)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /user/settings/security/two_factor/enroll. A fresh secret and QR
        -- code are shown; the first passcode proves the authenticator works. The scratch
        -- code is displayed once on success.
}

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/security/2fa.go:294
rule UserReenrolsTotp {
    when: UserReenrolsTotp(user, passcode)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    let twofa = TwoFactor{user: user}
    requires: exists twofa
    requires: enrolment_passcode_valid(user, passcode)

    ensures: twofa.last_used_passcode = null
    ensures: twofa.scratch_code_generation = twofa.scratch_code_generation + 1
    ensures: twofa.enrolled_at = now
    ensures: TotpEnrolled(user)
}

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/security/2fa.go:28
rule UserRegeneratesScratchCode {
    when: UserRegeneratesScratchCode(user)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    let twofa = TwoFactor{user: user}
    requires: exists twofa
    ensures: twofa.scratch_code_generation = twofa.scratch_code_generation + 1
}

-- Turning TOTP off is not possible while the instance requires 2FA of this user and it
-- is their last second factor.
-- decided: the last remaining second factor (TOTP, security key or passkey) cannot be
-- removed while 2FA is required; Forgejo refused TOTP even with a key left.
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/security/2fa.go:55
rule UserDisablesTotp {
    when: UserDisablesTotp(user)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    let twofa = TwoFactor{user: user}
    let login = UserLogin{user: user}
    requires: exists twofa
    requires: not login.requires_two_factor or login.has_security_keys

    ensures: not exists twofa
    ensures: TotpDisabled(user)
}

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/security/webauthn.go:65
rule UserRegistersSecurityKey {
    when: UserRegistersSecurityKey(user, name, attestation)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: not exists WebAuthnCredential{user: user, name: name}
    requires: webauthn_attestation_valid(user, attestation)

    ensures: WebAuthnCredential.created(user: user, name: name, discoverable: false, sign_count: 0, backup_eligible: false, backup_state: false, created_at: now)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/settings/security/webauthn/request_register then /register.
        -- An empty name defaults to a timestamp. Names compare case-insensitively.
}

-- Registering a passkey: a discoverable credential with user verification. It is a
-- second factor like any security key and also signs in on its own.
-- decided: passkeys (discoverable credentials) may be registered for passwordless sign-in.
rule UserRegistersPasskey {
    when: UserRegistersPasskey(user, name, attestation)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: not exists WebAuthnCredential{user: user, name: name}
    requires: webauthn_attestation_valid(user, attestation)
    requires: attestation_is_discoverable(attestation)

    ensures: WebAuthnCredential.created(user: user, name: name, discoverable: true, sign_count: 0, backup_eligible: false, backup_state: false, created_at: now)

    @guidance
        -- Same registration ceremony as a security key, asking for a resident key and
        -- user verification. An authenticator that cannot keep a resident credential
        -- is refused here and may still be registered as a security key.
}

-- decided: the last remaining second factor cannot be removed while 2FA is required.
-- from: routers/web/user/setting/security/webauthn.go:114
rule UserRemovesSecurityKey {
    when: UserRemovesSecurityKey(user, credential)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    -- read before the record goes: an emission sees the resulting state
    let key_name = credential.name
    let login = UserLogin{user: user}
    let keys = WebAuthnCredentials where user = user

    requires: credential.user = user
    requires: not login.requires_two_factor or login.has_totp or keys.count > 1

    ensures: not exists credential
    ensures: SecurityKeyRemoved(user: user, name: key_name)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: personal access tokens
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Repository-specific tokens: at least one repository, never public-only, and only the
-- issue / repository scope categories.
-- from: routers/api/v1/utils/access_token.go:136
rule UserCreatesAccessToken {
    when: UserCreatesAccessToken(actor, owner, name, scopes, public_only, all_repositories, repositories, via)
    requires: actor != owner or not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3; a site admin's token for someone else is admin console

    requires: actor = owner or actor.is_admin
    -- decided: with password Basic auth gone, a user mints their own tokens from a web
    -- session (or through the trusted proxy), never with another token.
    requires: actor != owner or via in {session, reverse_proxy}
    requires: name != ""
    requires: not exists AccessToken{owner: owner, name: name}
    requires: scopes.count > 0 or public_only
    requires: all_repositories or public_only = false
    requires: all_repositories or repositories.count > 0
    requires: all_repositories or scopes.all(sc => sc in {read_issue, write_issue, read_repository, write_repository})
    requires: all_repositories or repositories.all(r => can_read_code(actor, r))

    ensures:
        let token = AccessToken.created(
            owner: owner,
            name: name,
            scopes: scopes,
            public_only: public_only,
            all_repositories: all_repositories,
            repositories: repositories,
            last_eight: secret_suffix(),
            created_at: now,
            last_used_at: null
        )

    @guidance
        -- Web: /user/settings/applications/tokens/new (GET pre-fills from query).
        -- API: POST /users/{username}/tokens (reverse-proxy only for oneself — a token
        -- cannot mint tokens and password Basic auth no longer exists; or a site admin
        -- for anyone) and POST
        -- /admin/users/{username}/tokens (site admin, any credential). The secret is
        -- returned once. `all` expands to every write scope; unknown scope names are
        -- refused; duplicates are normalised away.
}

-- Regenerating replaces the secret, keeping name/scopes/repositories.
-- from: models/auth/access_token.go:246
rule UserRegeneratesAccessToken {
    when: UserRegeneratesAccessToken(user, token)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: token.owner = user
    ensures: token.last_eight = secret_suffix()
    ensures: token.last_used_at = null
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/utils/access_token.go:29
rule UserDeletesAccessToken {
    when: UserDeletesAccessToken(actor, token, via)
    requires: actor != token.owner or not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3; admin console stays writable

    requires: actor = token.owner or actor.is_admin
    requires: actor != token.owner or via in {session, reverse_proxy}

    let doomed = token
    ensures:
        for r in access/CredentialRestrictions where r.token = doomed:
            not exists r
    ensures: not exists token

    @guidance
        -- API: DELETE /users/{username}/tokens/{id-or-name} (a name matching several
        -- tokens is refused as ambiguous), DELETE /admin/users/{username}/tokens/{id}.
        -- Web: POST /user/settings/applications/tokens/delete.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: authenticating non-interactive requests (API, git, LFS, packages)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Methods are tried in order: OAuth2 bearer, HTTP signature (API only), access token,
-- Actions tokens, authorized-integration JWT, reverse proxy (if enabled), session (web).
-- The first that recognises its credential decides; a recognised but wrong credential
-- fails the request rather than falling through.
--
-- decided: tokens everywhere. `Authorization: Basic` with a username/e-mail and an
-- account password is refused on the API, git and LFS alike (Forgejo accepted it,
-- with X-Forgejo-OTP for TOTP users, and marked it FIXME for removal). The Basic
-- header still carries credentials: its password may be an access token, an OAuth2
-- access token or an integration JWT, which is how git clients authenticate.
-- from: services/auth/method/basic.go:24 (the method this replaces)
rule ClientPasswordBasicAuthRefused {
    when: ClientPresentsPassword(request, user, password)

    ensures: PasswordBasicAuthRefused(request: request)

    @guidance
        -- `Authorization: Basic` whose password is not a token is answered 401 with
        -- "password authentication is not supported, use an access token or OAuth2";
        -- nothing is authenticated and no credential is checked, so the answer does not
        -- reveal whether the password was right.
}

-- from: services/auth/method/access_token.go:31
rule ClientAuthenticatesWithAccessToken {
    when: ClientPresentsAccessToken(request, token)

    requires: UserLogin{user: token.owner}.may_use_account

    ensures: token.last_used_at = now
    ensures: RequestAuthenticated(user: token.owner, method: access_token)

    @guidance
        -- `Authorization: token <t>`, `Authorization: Bearer <t>`, or as the password
        -- (or username) of basic auth — the latter is how git over HTTP uses tokens
        -- (decided: the only Basic credential accepted).
        -- Git LFS accepts tokens only via basic auth. The request is then limited to the
        -- token's scopes, public-only flag and repository list (access.allium).
}

-- from: services/auth/method/oauth2.go:58
rule ClientAuthenticatesWithOAuth2Token {
    when: ClientPresentsOAuth2AccessToken(request, issuance)

    requires: config.oauth2_enabled
    requires: exists issuance.grant
    requires: issuance.access_valid
    requires: UserLogin{user: issuance.grant.user}.may_use_account

    ensures: RequestAuthenticated(user: issuance.grant.user, method: oauth2_bearer)

    @guidance
        -- Bearer, basic-password, or form `access_token`. A revoked grant kills every
        -- token issued under it. Effective scopes are the grant's token scopes, or every
        -- scope when the grant asked only for openid/profile/email/groups.
}

-- from: services/auth/method/httpsign.go:24
rule ClientAuthenticatesWithSignedRequest {
    when: ClientPresentsSignedRequest(request, key, via_certificate)

    requires: via_certificate = false or config.ssh_trusted_user_ca_keys_configured
    requires: http_signature_valid(request, key)
    requires: UserLogin{user: key.owner}.may_use_account

    ensures: RequestAuthenticated(user: key.owner, method: http_signature)

    @guidance
        -- API only. `Signature` header (HTTP signatures draft) made with a registered SSH
        -- key (looked up by fingerprint as keyId), or with an SSH certificate in
        -- X-Ssh-Certificate signed by a trusted user CA whose principal matches a key.
        -- A signature that does not verify is "not attempted", not a failure.
}

-- from: services/auth/method/reverseproxy.go:72
rule TrustedProxyAssertsUser {
    when: TrustedProxyAssertsUser(request, user, via_api)

    requires: config.enable_reverse_proxy_auth
    requires: via_api = false or config.enable_reverse_proxy_auth_api
    requires: request.via_trusted_proxy
    requires: UserLogin{user: user}.may_use_account

    ensures: RequestAuthenticated(user: user, method: reverse_proxy)

    @guidance
        -- The user is named in X-WEBAUTH-USER (or found by X-WEBAUTH-EMAIL when e-mail
        -- lookup is enabled). On web and git routes a session is created as well. Only
        -- requests from REVERSE_PROXY_TRUSTED_PROXIES are believed.
}

-- from: services/auth/method/reverseproxy.go:145
rule TrustedProxyRegistersUser {
    when: TrustedProxyRegistersUser(request, name, email, full_name)
    requires: not (exists accounts/ReservedName{name: name})   -- accounts: a reserved name is refused until an admin releases it
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: config.enable_reverse_proxy_auth
    requires: config.enable_reverse_proxy_auto_registration
    requires: request.via_trusted_proxy
    requires: username_available(name)

    ensures:
        let user = accounts/User.created(
            name: name,
            primary_email: email,
            kind: individual,
            is_active: true,
            is_admin: user_count() = 0,
            is_restricted: config.default_user_is_restricted,
            prohibit_login: false
        )
        UserLogin.created(user: user, source: null, login_name: name, has_password: false, must_change_password: false, password_changed_at: null, last_sign_in_at: now)
        UserSignedUp(user)
        RequestAuthenticated(user: user, method: reverse_proxy)

    @guidance
        -- E-mail comes from X-WEBAUTH-EMAIL when ENABLE_REVERSE_PROXY_EMAIL is on, else a
        -- random <uuid>@localhost; full name from X-WEBAUTH-FULLNAME when enabled.
}

-- from: services/auth/method/authorized_integration.go:60
rule ClientAuthenticatesWithIntegrationJwt {
    when: ClientPresentsIntegrationJwt(request, integration, claims)

    requires: jwt_signature_valid(integration.issuer, claims)
    requires: claims_satisfy(claims, integration.claim_rules)
    requires: UserLogin{user: integration.owner}.may_use_account

    ensures: RequestAuthenticated(user: integration.owner, method: integration_jwt)

    @guidance
        -- Bearer JWT (also accepted as basic-auth password on git and LFS routes). The
        -- integration is found by the JWT's exact `iss` and its single `aud`; claim rules
        -- are checked before any key is fetched; `iat`/`exp` are enforced. The request is
        -- then limited to the integration's scopes and repositories.
}

-- Site admins may act as another user on the API.
-- from: routers/api/v1/api.go:96
rule AdminSudoes {
    when: AdminSudoes(admin, target)
    requires: admin.is_admin
    ensures: RequestAuthenticated(user: target, method: session)

    @guidance
        -- `?sudo=<name>` or `Sudo: <name>` header on any API call. Non-admins get 403.
        -- The `method` passed on is the admin's own method in practice.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: authorized integrations (trusted external JWT issuers)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/auth/authorized_integration.go:223
rule UserCreatesAuthorizedIntegration {
    when: UserCreatesAuthorizedIntegration(user, name, ui, issuer, audience, claim_rules, scopes, public_only, all_repositories, repositories)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: not exists AuthorizedIntegration{issuer: issuer, audience: audience}
    requires: issuer_trustworthy(issuer)
    requires: claim_rules_well_formed(claim_rules)
    requires: all_repositories or public_only = false
    requires: all_repositories or repositories.count > 0
    requires: all_repositories or scopes.all(sc => sc in {read_issue, write_issue, read_repository, write_repository})
    requires: all_repositories or repositories.all(r => can_read_code(user, r))

    ensures: AuthorizedIntegration.created(owner: user, name: name, description: null, ui: ui, issuer: issuer, audience: audience, claim_rules: claim_rules, scopes: scopes, public_only: public_only, all_repositories: all_repositories, repositories: repositories, created_at: now)

    @guidance
        -- Web: /user/settings/authorized-integrations/{generic|forgejo-actions-local}/new.
        -- Every rule needs a claim; eq/glob need a value; in/glob_in need values (no empty
        -- glob, which would match anything); nest needs nested rules. External issuers
        -- are fetched under the [authorized_integration] host allow/block lists.
}

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/authorized_integrations.go:182
rule UserUpdatesAuthorizedIntegration {
    when: UserUpdatesAuthorizedIntegration(user, integration, claim_rules, scopes, public_only, all_repositories, repositories)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: integration.owner = user
    requires: claim_rules_well_formed(claim_rules)
    requires: all_repositories or public_only = false
    requires: all_repositories or repositories.count > 0
    ensures: integration.claim_rules = claim_rules
    ensures: integration.scopes = scopes
    ensures: integration.public_only = public_only
    ensures: integration.all_repositories = all_repositories
    ensures: integration.repositories = repositories
    -- its restriction follows the new reach and scopes
    ensures:
        for r in access/CredentialRestrictions where r.integration = integration:
            if not all_repositories:
                r.reach = listed_repositories
            else if public_only:
                r.reach = public_only
            else:
                r.reach = all_repositories
            r.listed = repositories
            r.has_admin_scope = scopes.any(sc => sc in {read_admin, write_admin})
}

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/authorized_integrations.go:418
rule UserDeletesAuthorizedIntegration {
    when: UserDeletesAuthorizedIntegration(user, integration)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: integration.owner = user
    let doomed = integration
    ensures:
        for r in access/CredentialRestrictions where r.integration = doomed:
            not exists r
    ensures: not exists integration
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: OAuth2 / OIDC provider — applications
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A user, an organisation owner, or a site admin (instance-wide) registers a client.
-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:265
rule OwnerRegistersOAuth2Application {
    when: OwnerRegistersOAuth2Application(actor, owner_user, owner_org, name, redirect_uris, confidential)
    requires: (owner_user = null and owner_org = null) or not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3; instance-wide apps are admin console

    requires: config.oauth2_enabled
    requires: owner_user = null or owner_org = null
    requires: owner_user = null or owner_user = actor
    requires: owner_org = null or is_org_owner(owner_org, actor)
    requires: owner_user != null or owner_org != null or actor.is_admin
    requires: name != ""
    requires: redirect_uris.count > 0
    requires: redirect_uris.all(u => valid_url(u))

    ensures: OAuth2Application.created(owner_user: owner_user, owner_org: owner_org, builtin: null, name: name, client_id: new_client_id(), confidential: confidential, redirect_uris: redirect_uris, created_at: now)

    @guidance
        -- Web: /user/settings/applications/oauth2, /org/{org}/settings/applications/oauth2,
        -- /admin/applications/oauth2. API: POST /user/applications/oauth2 (personal only).
        -- The client secret is shown once on creation.
}

-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:290
rule OwnerUpdatesOAuth2Application {
    when: OwnerUpdatesOAuth2Application(actor, app, name, redirect_uris, confidential)
    requires: app.is_instance_wide or not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3; instance-wide apps are admin console

    requires: may_manage_application(actor, app)
    requires: not app.is_builtin
    requires: redirect_uris.count > 0

    ensures: app.name = name
    ensures: app.redirect_uris = redirect_uris
    ensures: app.confidential = confidential

    @guidance
        -- API: PATCH /user/applications/oauth2/{id} also regenerates the secret.
}

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/oauth2_common.go:132
rule OwnerRegeneratesClientSecret {
    when: OwnerRegeneratesClientSecret(actor, app)
    requires: app.is_instance_wide or not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3; instance-wide apps are admin console
    requires: may_manage_application(actor, app)
    requires: not app.is_builtin
    ensures: ClientSecretRegenerated(app)
}

-- Deleting an application drops all its grants and outstanding codes.
-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:358
rule OwnerDeletesOAuth2Application {
    when: OwnerDeletesOAuth2Application(actor, app)
    requires: app.is_instance_wide or not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3; instance-wide apps are admin console

    requires: may_manage_application(actor, app)
    requires: not app.is_builtin

    ensures:
        for g in app.grants:
            for c in OAuth2AuthorizationCodes where grant = g:
                not exists c
            not exists g
    ensures: not exists app
}

-- The built-in public clients (git-credential-oauth, Git Credential Manager, tea) exist
-- exactly when listed in DEFAULT_APPLICATIONS; they are instance-wide and locked.
-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:86
rule BuiltinApplicationsReconciled {
    when: administration/InstanceStarted(instance)
    ensures:
        for b in config.oauth2_default_applications:
            if not exists OAuth2Application{builtin: b}:
                OAuth2Application.created(owner_user: null, owner_org: null, builtin: b, name: builtin_display_name(b), client_id: builtin_client_id(b), confidential: false, redirect_uris: {"http://127.0.0.1", "https://127.0.0.1"}, created_at: now)
    ensures:
        for app in OAuth2Applications where builtin != null:
            if app.builtin not in config.oauth2_default_applications:
                not exists app
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: OAuth2 / OIDC provider — authorization code flow
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The authorize endpoint. Public clients must use PKCE. A confidential client the user
-- has already granted the same scopes gets a code without asking again; different
-- scopes go back to the consent screen.
-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:423
rule UserRequestsAuthorization {
    when: UserRequestsAuthorization(user, app, redirect_uri, response_type, pkce_method, code_challenge, scopes, nonce)

    let grant = OAuth2Grant{user: user, application: app}

    requires: config.oauth2_enabled
    requires: redirect_uri_registered(app, redirect_uri)
    requires: response_type = "code"
    requires: app.confidential or pkce_method != none

    ensures:
        if app.confidential and exists grant and grant.scopes = scopes:
            OAuth2AuthorizationCode.created(grant: grant, redirect_uri: redirect_uri, code_challenge: code_challenge, pkce_method: pkce_method, issued_at: now, expires_at: now + config.oauth2_authorization_code_lifetime, status: issued)
            if nonce != null:
                grant.nonce = nonce
        else:
            ConsentRequested(user, app, redirect_uri, scopes)

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /login/oauth/authorize (sign-in required). Redirect URIs match
        -- exactly (case-insensitive, ignoring a trailing slash); for public clients an
        -- http loopback URI matches whatever port is used (RFC 8252). Unknown client or
        -- unregistered redirect URI → error page; other errors are redirected back to
        -- the client with error/error_description/state. The consent page names the
        -- application, its owner (or the instance) and the redirect target.
}

-- decided: re-consent replaces the scope. Approving sets the grant to exactly the
-- requested scopes; tokens already issued keep their scope until refreshed
-- (OAuth2TokenIssuance.scopes). Forgejo refused a grant with a different scope.
-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:595
rule UserGrantsConsent {
    when: UserGrantsConsent(user, app, redirect_uri, scopes, pkce_method, code_challenge, nonce)

    let existing = OAuth2Grant{user: user, application: app}

    requires: config.oauth2_enabled
    requires: redirect_uri_registered(app, redirect_uri)

    ensures:
        if exists existing:
            existing.scopes = scopes
            OAuth2AuthorizationCode.created(grant: existing, redirect_uri: redirect_uri, code_challenge: code_challenge, pkce_method: pkce_method, issued_at: now, expires_at: now + config.oauth2_authorization_code_lifetime, status: issued)
        else:
            let grant = OAuth2Grant.created(user: user, application: app, scopes: scopes, nonce: nonce, counter: 1, created_at: now)
            OAuth2AuthorizationCode.created(grant: grant, redirect_uri: redirect_uri, code_challenge: code_challenge, pkce_method: pkce_method, issued_at: now, expires_at: now + config.oauth2_authorization_code_lifetime, status: issued)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /login/oauth/grant. client_id/state/redirect_uri must match what the
        -- authorize step stored in the session. The consent page lists the requested
        -- scopes; approving a grant that existed with other scopes replaces them.
}

-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:603
rule UserDeniesConsent {
    when: UserDeniesConsent(user, app, redirect_uri)
    requires: redirect_uri_registered(app, redirect_uri)
    ensures: AuthorizationDenied(user, app)
}

-- The token endpoint, authorization_code grant. The code is single-use.
-- decided: codes live oauth2_authorization_code_lifetime (10 minutes, configurable) and
-- are redeemed at most once (Forgejo never set their expiry).
-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:844
rule ClientExchangesAuthorizationCode {
    when: ClientExchangesAuthorizationCode(app, client_secret_valid, code, code_verifier, redirect_uri)

    requires: config.oauth2_enabled
    requires: app.confidential = false or client_secret_valid
    requires: code.status = issued
    requires: code.grant.application = app
    requires: code.redirect_uri = redirect_uri
    requires: pkce_verifier_matches(code, code_verifier)

    let grant = code.grant

    ensures: code.status = redeemed
    ensures: grant.counter = grant.counter + 1
    ensures: OAuth2TokenIssuance.created(grant: grant, scopes: grant.scopes, refresh_counter: grant.counter, access_expires_at: now + config.oauth2_access_token_lifetime, refresh_expires_at: now + config.oauth2_refresh_token_lifetime, includes_id_token: "openid" in grant.scopes, issued_at: now)

    @guidance
        -- POST /login/oauth/access_token (CORS-enabled, no CSRF). Client credentials in
        -- the body or HTTP basic; if both, they must agree. A replayed code fails because
        -- it was deleted on first use. With PKCE S256 the verifier's SHA-256 must equal
        -- the challenge; `plain` compares directly; a challenge with no verifier fails.
        -- The id_token (openid scope) carries iss=<app url>, aud=client_id, sub=user id,
        -- nonce, and name/preferred_username/profile/picture/website/locale/updated_at
        -- (profile), email/email_verified (email), groups "org" and "org:team" (groups).
        -- With a symmetric signing key the id_token is signed with the client secret.
}

-- The token endpoint, refresh_token grant. Each refresh token works once.
-- from: routers/web/auth/oauth.go:763
rule ClientRefreshesToken {
    when: ClientRefreshesToken(app, client_secret_valid, previous)

    requires: config.oauth2_enabled
    requires: app.confidential = false or client_secret_valid
    requires: previous.grant.application = app
    requires: previous.refresh_usable

    let grant = previous.grant

    ensures: grant.counter = grant.counter + 1
    ensures: OAuth2TokenIssuance.created(grant: grant, scopes: grant.scopes, refresh_counter: grant.counter, access_expires_at: now + config.oauth2_access_token_lifetime, refresh_expires_at: now + config.oauth2_refresh_token_lifetime, includes_id_token: "openid" in grant.scopes, issued_at: now)

    @guidance
        -- A refresh token presented a second time ("already used") is refused and logged
        -- as a possible replay; with INVALIDATE_REFRESH_TOKENS off they stay reusable
        -- until expiry.
}

-- from: routers/web/user/setting/oauth2_common.go:168
rule UserRevokesGrant {
    when: UserRevokesGrant(user, grant)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)

    requires: grant.user = user

    ensures:
        for c in OAuth2AuthorizationCodes where grant = grant:
            not exists c
    ensures: not exists grant

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /user/settings/applications/oauth2/{id}/revoke/{grantId}. All access
        -- and refresh tokens issued under the grant stop working immediately.
}

-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:389
rule AuthorizationCodeExpires {
    when: auth_code: OAuth2AuthorizationCode.expires_at <= now
    requires: auth_code.status = issued
    ensures: auth_code.status = expired
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: authentication sources (site admin)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: routers/web/admin/auths.go:203
rule AdminCreatesAuthSource {
    when: AdminCreatesAuthSource(admin, name, kind, is_active, sync_enabled, settings)

    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: name != ""
    requires: not exists AuthSource{name: name}
    requires: kind != remote
    requires: kind != oauth2 or settings.provider != "openidConnect" or http_url(settings.openid_discovery_url)
    requires: kind != oauth2 or is_active = false or provider_initialisable(settings)

    ensures: AuthSource.created(name: name, kind: kind, is_active: is_active, sync_enabled: sync_enabled and kind in {ldap_bind_dn, ldap_simple}, settings: settings, created_at: now)

    @guidance
        -- Web: /admin/auths/new. LDAP bind passwords and OAuth2 client secrets are stored
        -- encrypted and never shown back. An active OAuth2 source is registered with the
        -- provider library immediately; if that fails (e.g. OIDC discovery unreachable)
        -- the source is not saved.
}

-- from: routers/web/admin/auths.go:314
rule AdminUpdatesAuthSource {
    when: AdminUpdatesAuthSource(admin, source, name, is_active, sync_enabled, settings)

    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: name != ""
    requires: name = source.name or not exists AuthSource{name: name}
    requires: source.kind != oauth2 or is_active = false or provider_initialisable(settings)

    ensures: source.name = name
    ensures: source.is_active = is_active
    ensures: source.sync_enabled = (sync_enabled and source.is_ldap)
    ensures: source.settings = settings
}

-- A source still used by any account (as its password source or as a linked external
-- login) cannot be deleted.
-- from: services/auth/source.go:14
rule AdminDeletesAuthSource {
    when: AdminDeletesAuthSource(admin, source)

    requires: admin.is_admin
    requires: not source.in_use

    ensures:
        for t in LongTermAuthorizations where sso_source = source:
            not exists t
    ensures: AuthSourceDeleted(source)
    ensures: not exists source

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /admin/auths/{id}/delete; "still in use" is shown as a flash.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: scheduled directory synchronisation
------------------------------------------------------------

-- administration's sync_external_users cron task ran (on its schedule or "run now").
-- from: services/cron/tasks_basic.go:90
rule ScheduledExternalUserSync {
    when: administration/ExternalUserSyncDue(update_existing)
    ensures:
        for source in AuthSources where is_active = true and sync_enabled = true:
            AuthSourceSyncRequested(source: source, update_existing: update_existing)
    ensures: ExternalUserSyncFinished()   -- decided: requests 5 (the owner reports the run done)
}

-- The admin dashboard's "synchronise external user data" button.
-- from: routers/web/admin/admin.go:162
rule AdminRunsExternalUserSync {
    when: AdminRunsExternalUserSync(admin)

    requires: admin.is_admin

    ensures:
        for source in AuthSources where is_active = true and sync_enabled = true:
            AuthSourceSyncRequested(source: source, update_existing: config.sync_external_users_update_existing)
}

-- Synchronise one LDAP source against its directory: create missing accounts, refresh
-- existing ones, deactivate accounts whose entry disappeared.
-- from: services/auth/source/ldap/source_sync.go:17
rule LdapSourceSynchronised {
    when: AuthSourceSyncRequested(source, update_existing)

    let src = source
    requires: src.is_ldap
    let entries = DirectoryEntries where source = src
    requires: entries.count > 0 or src.settings.allow_deactivate_all

    ensures:
        for e in entries:
            if not exists UserLogin{source: src, login_name: e.username} and not (exists accounts/ReservedName{name: e.username}):
                let user = accounts/User.created(
                    name: e.username,
                    primary_email: e.email,
                    kind: individual,
                    is_active: true,
                    is_admin: e.is_admin,
                    is_restricted: e.is_restricted,
                    prohibit_login: false
                )
                UserLogin.created(user: user, source: src, login_name: e.username, has_password: false, must_change_password: false, password_changed_at: null, last_sign_in_at: null)
                UserSignedUp(user)
                ExternalSshKeysAsserted(user: user, source: src, keys: e.ssh_public_keys)
                if src.settings.groups_enabled:
                    ExternalGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: src, groups: e.groups)
                    ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted(user: user, source: src, groups: e.groups)
    -- decided: requests 7 — with group lookup on, the sync re-asserts every
    -- account's group memberships, as a sign-in does (team and quota groups)
    ensures:
        if src.settings.groups_enabled:
            for login in UserLogins where source = src:
                if exists DirectoryEntry{source: src, username: login.login_name}:
                    ExternalGroupsAsserted(user: login.user, source: src, groups: DirectoryEntry{source: src, username: login.login_name}.groups)
                    ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted(user: login.user, source: src, groups: DirectoryEntry{source: src, username: login.login_name}.groups)
    ensures:
        if update_existing:
            for login in UserLogins where source = src:
                if exists DirectoryEntry{source: src, username: login.login_name}:
                    login.user.is_active = true
                    ExternalAdminFlagsAsserted(user: login.user, is_admin: DirectoryEntry{source: src, username: login.login_name}.is_admin, is_restricted: DirectoryEntry{source: src, username: login.login_name}.is_restricted)
                    ExternalSshKeysAsserted(user: login.user, source: src, keys: DirectoryEntry{source: src, username: login.login_name}.ssh_public_keys)
    ensures:
        for login in UserLogins where source = src:
            if not exists DirectoryEntry{source: src, username: login.login_name}:
                login.user.is_active = false

    @guidance
        -- Existing accounts get full name, primary e-mail, admin (only when an admin filter
        -- is set) and restricted (only when a restricted filter is set and the user is not
        -- admin) refreshed. Users are matched by login name, then by e-mail. If the search
        -- returns nothing and allow_deactivate_all is off, the sync is refused rather than
        -- deactivating everyone (LdapSourceSyncRefused).
}

-- A directory search that found nobody, on a source that may not deactivate
-- everyone, refuses the sync; the operator is told.
-- decided: requests 8 — a refused LDAP sync leaves a system notice for admins.
rule LdapSourceSyncRefused {
    when: AuthSourceSyncRequested(source, update_existing)
    requires: source.is_ldap
    requires: (DirectoryEntries where source = source).count = 0
    requires: not source.settings.allow_deactivate_all
    ensures: ExternalUserSyncRefused(source: source)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: what a token's restriction is (access reduces permissions by it)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Every access token carries the reach access/CredentialRestriction describes:
-- a repository-specific token reaches its listed repositories, a public-only
-- token public things, any other token everything; the admin scope category
-- (read:admin / write:admin, or `all`) is what lets a site administrator act as
-- one through it (decided: access 5). Tokens are never edited, only
-- regenerated (same restriction) or deleted (restriction removed with them).
-- from: services/authz/authorization_reducer.go:11
rule AccessTokenRestrictionDerived {
    when: token: AccessToken.created
    -- (each reach is written as its own creation: a value chosen inside an
    -- `if` expression is not read as the target field's state)
    let admin_scoped = token.scopes.any(sc => sc in {read_admin, write_admin})
    ensures:
        if not token.all_repositories:
            access/CredentialRestriction.created(token: token, integration: null, reach: listed_repositories,
                listed: token.repositories, has_admin_scope: admin_scoped)
        else if token.public_only:
            access/CredentialRestriction.created(token: token, integration: null, reach: public_only,
                listed: token.repositories, has_admin_scope: admin_scoped)
        else:
            access/CredentialRestriction.created(token: token, integration: null, reach: all_repositories,
                listed: token.repositories, has_admin_scope: admin_scoped)
}

-- An authorized integration's JWTs carry the same kind of reach, derived the
-- same way from the integration's repositories, public-only flag and scopes.
rule AuthorizedIntegrationRestrictionDerived {
    when: integration: AuthorizedIntegration.created
    let admin_scoped = integration.scopes.any(sc => sc in {read_admin, write_admin})
    ensures:
        if not integration.all_repositories:
            access/CredentialRestriction.created(token: null, integration: integration, reach: listed_repositories,
                listed: integration.repositories, has_admin_scope: admin_scoped)
        else if integration.public_only:
            access/CredentialRestriction.created(token: null, integration: integration, reach: public_only,
                listed: integration.repositories, has_admin_scope: admin_scoped)
        else:
            access/CredentialRestriction.created(token: null, integration: integration, reach: all_repositories,
                listed: integration.repositories, has_admin_scope: admin_scoped)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: acts administration asks for (admin console and CLI)
------------------------------------------------------------

-- `forgejo admin user reset-mfa` and the admin edit form's "reset 2FA": every
-- second factor goes, TOTP, security keys and passkeys alike.
-- from: routers/web/admin/users.go:466
rule AdminResetRemovesSecondFactors {
    when: administration/UserTwoFactorResetByAdmin(admin, user)
    ensures:
        for t in TwoFactors where user = user:
            not exists t
        for c in WebAuthnCredentials where user = user:
            not exists c
}

-- An administrator rebound an account to a login source and login name: the
-- login record is the one place that binding lives (decided: requests 4).
rule RebindLoginForAdmin {
    when: administration/UserLoginSourceSetByAdmin(admin, user, login_source, login_name)
    let login = UserLogin{user: user}
    requires: exists login
    ensures: login.source = login_source
    ensures: login.login_name = login_name
}

-- A password set by an administrator or the operator is stored like any other:
-- every remember-me record dies with the old password, and the user gets the
-- password-changed security mail.
-- from: models/user/user.go:452, services/user/update.go:202
rule AdminSetPasswordRetiresOldDevices {
    when: administration/UserPasswordSetByAdmin(admin, user, password)
    ensures:
        for t in LongTermAuthorizations where user = user and status = active:
            t.status = revoked
    ensures: PasswordChanged(user: user)
}

-- from: cmd/admin_user_change_password.go:114
rule OperatorSetPasswordRetiresOldDevices {
    when: administration/UserPasswordSetByOperator(operator, user, password)
    ensures:
        for t in LongTermAuthorizations where user = user and status = active:
            t.status = revoked
    ensures: PasswordChanged(user: user)
}

-- A token minted for a user by a site admin (API) or the operator (CLI
-- `generate-access-token`, `user create --access-token`): every repository,
-- not public-only.
-- from: routers/api/v1/admin/user_token.go:46, cmd/admin_user_generate_access_token.go:48
rule AccessTokenIssuedForUser {
    when: administration/AccessTokenRequestedForUser(requester, user, token_name, scopes)
    requires: token_name != ""
    requires: scopes.count > 0
    requires: not exists AccessToken{owner: user, name: token_name}
    ensures: AccessToken.created(owner: user, name: token_name, scopes: scopes, public_only: false, all_repositories: true, repositories: {}, last_eight: secret_suffix(), created_at: now, last_used_at: null)
    @guidance
        -- The secret is printed once on the operator's terminal or returned once
        -- by the API. `all` expands to every write scope.
}

-- `forgejo admin user create-authorized-integration`: the same checks as the
-- settings page; the audience is generated and printed.
-- from: cmd/admin_user_generate_authorized_integration.go:102
rule AuthorizedIntegrationCreatedFromCli {
    when: administration/AuthorizedIntegrationRequested(operator, user, name, description, issuer, claim_rules, scopes, all_repositories, repositories)
    let audience = new_integration_audience()
    requires: name != ""
    requires: issuer_trustworthy(issuer)
    requires: claim_rules_well_formed(claim_rules)
    requires: all_repositories or repositories.count > 0
    requires: all_repositories or scopes.all(sc => sc in {read_issue, write_issue, read_repository, write_repository})
    requires: not exists AuthorizedIntegration{issuer: issuer, audience: audience}
    ensures: AuthorizedIntegration.created(owner: user, name: name, description: description, ui: generic, issuer: issuer, audience: audience, claim_rules: claim_rules, scopes: scopes, public_only: false, all_repositories: all_repositories, repositories: repositories, created_at: now)
}

-- `forgejo admin auth add-oauth|add-ldap|add-ldap-simple|add-pam|add-smtp`:
-- the same validation as the admin form.
-- from: cmd/admin_auth_oauth.go, cmd/admin_auth_ldap.go, services/auth/source.go:14
rule AuthSourceAddedFromCli {
    when: administration/AuthSourceConfiguredFromCli(operator, kind, action, source, name, is_active, sync_enabled, settings)
    requires: action = add
    requires: name != ""
    requires: not exists AuthSource{name: name}
    requires: kind != oauth2 or settings.provider != "openidConnect" or http_url(settings.openid_discovery_url)
    requires: kind != oauth2 or is_active = false or provider_initialisable(settings)
    ensures: AuthSource.created(name: name, kind: kind, is_active: is_active, sync_enabled: sync_enabled and kind in {ldap_bind_dn, ldap_simple}, settings: settings, created_at: now)
}

-- `forgejo admin auth update-oauth|update-ldap|...` (by source id).
rule AuthSourceUpdatedFromCli {
    when: administration/AuthSourceConfiguredFromCli(operator, kind, action, source, name, is_active, sync_enabled, settings)
    requires: action = update
    requires: source != null
    requires: source.kind = kind
    requires: name = source.name or not exists AuthSource{name: name}
    requires: kind != oauth2 or is_active = false or provider_initialisable(settings)
    ensures: source.name = name
    ensures: source.is_active = is_active
    ensures: source.sync_enabled = (sync_enabled and source.is_ldap)
    ensures: source.settings = settings
}

-- `forgejo admin auth delete --id`: refused while the source is in use.
rule AuthSourceDeletedFromCli {
    when: administration/AuthSourceConfiguredFromCli(operator, kind, action, source, name, is_active, sync_enabled, settings)
    requires: action = delete
    requires: source != null
    requires: not source.in_use
    ensures:
        for t in LongTermAuthorizations where sso_source = source:
            not exists t
    ensures: AuthSourceDeleted(source: source)
    ensures: not exists source
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: account removal
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A purge ends every session of the account immediately.
-- from: services/user/user.go:183
rule PurgedUserSessionsEnd {
    when: accounts/UserPurged(user)

    ensures:
        for s in Sessions where user = user and status = authenticated:
            s.status = destroyed
    ensures:
        for t in LongTermAuthorizations where user = user and status = active:
            t.status = revoked
}

-- from: models/auth/oauth2.go:647
rule DeletedUserLosesCredentials {
    when: accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, kind, purge, delete_contributions)

    ensures:
        for r in access/CredentialRestrictions where r.token != null and r.token.owner = user:
            not exists r
        for r in access/CredentialRestrictions where r.integration != null and r.integration.owner = user:
            not exists r
        for t in AccessTokens where owner = user:
            not exists t
        for t in TwoFactors where user = user:
            not exists t
        for c in WebAuthnCredentials where user = user:
            not exists c
        for l in ExternalLogins where user = user:
            not exists l
        for o in OpenIDIdentities where user = user:
            not exists o
        for g in OAuth2Grants where user = user:
            not exists g
        for a in OAuth2Applications where owner_user = user:
            not exists a
        for i in AuthorizedIntegrations where owner = user:
            not exists i
        for t in LongTermAuthorizations where user = user:
            not exists t
        for c in EmailVerificationCodes where user = user:
            not exists c
        for l in UserLogins where user = user:
            not exists l
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant UniqueAuthSourceName {
    for a in AuthSources:
        for b in AuthSources:
            (a != b) implies a.name != b.name
}

invariant UniqueAccessTokenNamePerOwner {
    for a in AccessTokens:
        for b in AccessTokens:
            (a != b and a.owner = b.owner) implies a.name != b.name
}

invariant RepositoryScopedTokensAreNarrow {
    for t in AccessTokens:
        (not t.all_repositories) implies (t.repositories.count > 0 and not t.public_only and t.scopes.all(s => s in {read_issue, write_issue, read_repository, write_repository}))
}

invariant AtMostOneTotpPerUser {
    for a in TwoFactors:
        for b in TwoFactors:
            (a != b) implies a.user != b.user
}

invariant UniqueSecurityKeyNamePerUser {
    for a in WebAuthnCredentials:
        for b in WebAuthnCredentials:
            (a != b and a.user = b.user) implies a.name != b.name
}

invariant OneLoginPerUser {
    for a in UserLogins:
        for b in UserLogins:
            (a != b) implies a.user != b.user
}

invariant UniqueExternalIdentity {
    for a in ExternalLogins:
        for b in ExternalLogins:
            (a != b and a.source = b.source) implies a.external_id != b.external_id
}

invariant UniqueOpenID {
    for a in OpenIDIdentities:
        for b in OpenIDIdentities:
            (a != b) implies a.uri != b.uri
}

invariant UniqueClientId {
    for a in OAuth2Applications:
        for b in OAuth2Applications:
            (a != b) implies a.client_id != b.client_id
}

invariant ApplicationHasAtMostOneOwner {
    for a in OAuth2Applications:
        a.owner_user = null or a.owner_org = null
}

invariant BuiltinApplicationsArePublicAndInstanceWide {
    for a in OAuth2Applications:
        a.is_builtin implies (a.is_instance_wide and not a.confidential)
}

invariant OneGrantPerUserAndApplication {
    for a in OAuth2Grants:
        for b in OAuth2Grants:
            (a != b and a.user = b.user) implies a.application != b.application
}

invariant UniqueIntegrationIssuerAudience {
    for a in AuthorizedIntegrations:
        for b in AuthorizedIntegrations:
            (a != b and a.issuer = b.issuer) implies a.audience != b.audience
}

invariant SyncOnlyForLdap {
    for s in AuthSources:
        s.sync_enabled implies s.is_ldap
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A browser session nobody has signed in to yet. Not access/Visitor (a party
-- behind one request): the sign-in flows act on the anonymous session itself.
actor AnonymousSession {
    identified_by: Session where status = anonymous
}

-- A browser session that passed the password step and owes a second factor.
actor SecondFactorChallenger {
    identified_by: Session where status = pending_second_factor
}

-- Signed-in users and site administrators are access/SignedInUser and
-- access/SiteAdmin.

-- Signed in but not yet activated: may only use the activation page.
actor InactiveUser {
    identified_by: accounts/User where is_active = false and prohibit_login = false
}

-- A program on the other end of an HTTP request carrying some credential.
actor CredentialBearer {
    identified_by: ClientRequest where carries_credentials = true
}

-- A front proxy the instance has been told to trust for identity headers.
actor TrustedReverseProxy {
    identified_by: ClientRequest where via_trusted_proxy = true
}

-- A registered OAuth2 client talking to the token / introspection endpoints.
actor OAuth2Client {
    identified_by: OAuth2Application where client_id != ""
}

-- An external identity provider delivering the sign-in callback.
actor IdentityProvider {
    identified_by: AuthSource where kind = oauth2 and is_active = true
}

-- An incoming HTTP request, as far as authentication can tell.
-- from: services/auth/interface.go:26
external entity ClientRequest {
    carries_credentials: Boolean
    method: CredentialMethod?           -- which kind of credential it carries
    via_trusted_proxy: Boolean
    from_git_client: Boolean
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The sign-in / sign-up / recovery pages for somebody not signed in.
surface SignInPage {
    facing visitor: AnonymousSession

    exposes:
        config.enable_internal_signin
        config.show_registration_button
        config.enable_captcha
        config.captcha_kind
        config.enable_openid_signin
        config.mail_service_configured
        for source in AuthSources where kind = oauth2 and is_active = true:
            source.name
            source.settings.icon_url

    provides:
        VisitorSignsInWithPassword(visitor, user, password, remember)
            when config.enable_internal_signin
        VisitorSignsInWithPasskey(visitor, credential, sign_count, remember)
            when config.enable_internal_signin
        VisitorSignsInWithExternalPassword(visitor, source, entry, password)
            when config.enable_internal_signin
        VisitorRegisters(visitor, name, email, password)
            when not config.disable_registration and not config.allow_only_external_registration
        VisitorStartsProviderSignIn(visitor, source, prompt_none)
        VisitorResumesWithRememberMe(visitor, lta)
        VisitorSignsInWithOpenID(visitor, uri)
            when config.enable_openid_signin
        VisitorConnectsOpenIDToAccount(visitor, user, password)
            when visitor.pending_openid_uri != null
        VisitorRequestsPasswordReset(visitor, user)
            when config.mail_service_configured
        VisitorLinksPendingIdentityBySignIn(visitor, user, password, remember)
            when visitor.pending_external_identity != null
        VisitorRegistersFromPendingIdentity(visitor, name, email, password)
            when visitor.pending_external_identity != null and not config.disable_registration

    @guarantee SameAnswerForUnknownAccounts
        -- Wrong password, unknown user and unactivated e-mail produce the same message;
        -- the reset form says "mail sent" whether or not the address exists.

    @guidance
        -- Web: /user/login, /user/sign_up, /user/login/openid, /user/openid/connect,
        -- /user/openid/register, /user/link_account, /user/link_account_signin,
        -- /user/link_account_signup, /user/forgot_password, /user/oauth2/{source}.
        -- A signed-in visitor opening these is redirected to `redirect_to` or home.
}

surface SecondFactorChallenge {
    facing session: SecondFactorChallenger

    exposes:
        UserLogin{user: session.pending_user}.has_totp
        UserLogin{user: session.pending_user}.has_security_keys

    provides:
        VisitorCompletesTotpChallenge(session, passcode)
        VisitorUsesScratchCode(session, scratch_code)
        VisitorCompletesWebAuthnChallenge(session, credential, sign_count)

    @guidance
        -- Web: /user/two_factor, /user/two_factor/scratch, /user/webauthn,
        -- /user/webauthn/assertion.
}

-- Following a mailed link (activation, reset, e-mail confirmation).
surface MailedCodeLanding {
    facing visitor: Session

    context code: EmailVerificationCode

    exposes:
        code.purpose
        code.is_valid
        code.user.primary_email

    provides:
        UserActivatesAccount(visitor, code, password)
            when code.purpose = user_activation and code.is_valid
        VisitorResetsPassword(visitor, code, new_password, passcode, scratch_code)
            when code.purpose = password_reset and code.is_valid
        UserConfirmsEmailAddress(code, email)
            when code.purpose = email_activation and code.is_valid

    timeout:
        VerificationCodeExpires

    @guidance
        -- Web: /user/activate?code=, /user/recover_account?code=, /user/activate_email.
}

surface AccountActivation {
    facing user: InactiveUser

    exposes:
        user.primary_email
        config.activation_code_lifetime
        config.register_manual_confirm
        exists MailSendThrottle{user: user, kind: resend}

    provides:
        InactiveUserRequestsActivationMail(user)
            when config.register_email_confirm and not exists MailSendThrottle{user: user, kind: resend}
        InactiveUserReplacesUnconfirmedEmail(user, email)
            when config.register_email_confirm
        UserSignsOut(session)

    timeout:
        MailThrottleLapses
}

-- Security settings of the signed-in user.
surface SecuritySettings {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser

    let login = UserLogin{user: user}

    exposes:
        login.has_totp
        login.requires_two_factor
        login.must_change_password
        login.is_local
        for key in WebAuthnCredentials where user = user:
            key.name
            key.discoverable
            key.created_at
        for link in ExternalLogins where user = user:
            link.source.name
            link.provider
            link.email
        for oid in OpenIDIdentities where user = user:
            oid.uri
            oid.show_publicly

    provides:
        UserChangesPassword(user, old_password, new_password)
            when not user.has_feature_disabled(manage_password)
        UserChangesForcedPassword(user, new_password)
            when login.must_change_password
        UserEnrolsTotp(user, passcode)
            when not login.has_totp
        UserReenrolsTotp(user, passcode)
            when login.has_totp
        UserRegeneratesScratchCode(user)
            when login.has_totp
        UserDisablesTotp(user)
            when login.has_totp and (not login.requires_two_factor or login.has_security_keys)
        UserRegistersSecurityKey(user, name, attestation)
        UserRegistersPasskey(user, name, attestation)
        UserRemovesSecurityKey(user, key)
        UserUnlinksExternalLogin(user, link)
        UserAddsOpenID(user, uri)
            when config.enable_openid_signin
        UserRemovesOpenID(user, oid)
        UserTogglesOpenIDVisibility(user, oid)
        VisitorStartsProviderSignIn(session, source, prompt_none)
        UserSignsOut(session)

    @guarantee TwoFactorEnrolmentAlwaysReachable
        -- When 2FA is required and missing, every other page redirects here and the
        -- navigation is hidden until a factor is enrolled.

    @guidance
        -- Web: /user/settings/security (+ /two_factor/*, /webauthn/*, /openid/*,
        -- /account_link), /user/settings/account (password), /user/settings/change_password.
}

-- Applications settings: tokens, own OAuth2 apps, granted apps.
surface ApplicationSettings {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser

    exposes:
        for token in AccessTokens where owner = user:
            token.name
            token.scopes
            token.public_only
            token.repositories
            token.last_eight
            token.created_at
            token.has_recent_activity
            token.has_been_used
        for app in OAuth2Applications where owner_user = user:
            app.name
            app.client_id
            app.confidential
            app.redirect_uris
        for grant in OAuth2Grants where user = user:
            grant.application.name
            grant.scopes
            grant.created_at
        for integration in AuthorizedIntegrations where owner = user:
            integration.name
            integration.issuer
            integration.audience
            integration.claim_rules
            integration.scopes

    provides:
        UserCreatesAccessToken(user, user, name, scopes, public_only, all_repositories, repositories, via)
        UserRegeneratesAccessToken(user, token)
        UserDeletesAccessToken(user, token, via)
        OwnerRegistersOAuth2Application(user, user, owner_org, name, redirect_uris, confidential)
            when config.oauth2_enabled
        OwnerUpdatesOAuth2Application(user, app, name, redirect_uris, confidential)
        OwnerRegeneratesClientSecret(user, app)
        OwnerDeletesOAuth2Application(user, app)
        UserRevokesGrant(user, grant)
        UserCreatesAuthorizedIntegration(user, name, ui, issuer, audience, claim_rules, scopes, public_only, all_repositories, repositories)
        UserUpdatesAuthorizedIntegration(user, integration, claim_rules, scopes, public_only, all_repositories, repositories)
        UserDeletesAuthorizedIntegration(user, integration)

    @guarantee TokenSecretShownOnce
        -- The full token / client secret is revealed only in the response that created
        -- or regenerated it.

    @guidance
        -- Web: /user/settings/applications, /tokens/new, /tokens/delete,
        -- /tokens/regenerate, /oauth2/{id}, /oauth2/{id}/regenerate_secret,
        -- /oauth2/{id}/delete, /oauth2/{id}/revoke/{grantId},
        -- /user/settings/authorized-integrations/*.
        -- API: GET/POST /users/{username}/tokens, DELETE /users/{username}/tokens/{id},
        -- GET/POST /user/applications/oauth2, GET/PATCH/DELETE /user/applications/oauth2/{id}.
        -- Token listings show repositories only where the viewer can still see them.
}

surface OrganizationOAuth2Applications {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser

    context org: organizations/Organization

    exposes:
        for app in OAuth2Applications where owner_org = org:
            app.name
            app.client_id
            app.confidential
            app.redirect_uris

    provides:
        OwnerRegistersOAuth2Application(user, owner_user, org, name, redirect_uris, confidential)
            when is_org_owner(org, user) and config.oauth2_enabled
        OwnerUpdatesOAuth2Application(user, app, name, redirect_uris, confidential)
            when is_org_owner(org, user)
        OwnerRegeneratesClientSecret(user, app)
            when is_org_owner(org, user)
        OwnerDeletesOAuth2Application(user, app)
            when is_org_owner(org, user)

    @guidance
        -- Web: /org/{org}/settings/applications(/oauth2/{id}...). Org owners only.
}

-- The consent screen of the OAuth2 provider.
surface OAuth2Consent {
    facing user: access/SignedInUser

    context app: OAuth2Application

    exposes:
        app.name
        app.owner_user.name
        app.owner_org.name
        app.is_instance_wide

    provides:
        UserRequestsAuthorization(user, app, redirect_uri, response_type, pkce_method, code_challenge, scopes, nonce)
            when config.oauth2_enabled
        UserGrantsConsent(user, app, redirect_uri, scopes, pkce_method, code_challenge, nonce)
            when config.oauth2_enabled
        UserDeniesConsent(user, app, redirect_uri)

    @guidance
        -- Web: /login/oauth/authorize, /login/oauth/grant.
}

-- Endpoints a registered client calls directly.
surface OAuth2ClientEndpoints {
    facing client: OAuth2Client

    exposes:
        client.client_id
        config.oauth2_access_token_lifetime
        for grant in client.grants:
            grant.user.name
            grant.scopes

    provides:
        ClientExchangesAuthorizationCode(client, client_secret_valid, code, code_verifier, redirect_uri)
            when config.oauth2_enabled
        ClientRefreshesToken(client, client_secret_valid, previous)
            when config.oauth2_enabled

    @guarantee IntrospectionNeedsClientCredentials
        -- POST /login/oauth/introspect answers {active, scope, username, iss, aud, sub,
        -- exp} only to a caller presenting valid client credentials via basic auth;
        -- an invalid token yields active=false, never an error.

    @guidance
        -- /login/oauth/access_token, /login/oauth/introspect, /login/oauth/keys (JWKS),
        -- /.well-known/openid-configuration (issuer = app URL, code flow only),
        -- /login/oauth/userinfo (OAuth2 bearer only: sub, name, preferred_username,
        -- email, picture, groups; groups omit private org memberships unless the grant
        -- has read:organization / read:admin / all and additional grant scopes are on).
}

-- Whatever presents credentials on API, git-over-HTTP, LFS and package routes.
surface RequestAuthentication {
    facing caller: CredentialBearer

    provides:
        ClientPresentsPassword(caller, user, password)
        ClientPresentsAccessToken(caller, token)
        ClientPresentsOAuth2AccessToken(caller, issuance)
            when config.oauth2_enabled
        ClientPresentsSignedRequest(caller, key, via_certificate)
        ClientPresentsIntegrationJwt(caller, integration, claims)
        AdminSudoes(admin, target)

    @guarantee AccountGateApplies
        -- Whatever the credential, an inactive (when e-mail confirmation is on), login-
        -- prohibited, must-change-password or missing-required-2FA account is refused
        -- with 403 and a reason; REQUIRE_SIGNIN_VIEW refuses anonymous API calls.

    @guidance
        -- Order of methods per route family:
        --   API: OAuth2, HTTP signature, access token, Actions tokens, integration JWT,
        --        reverse proxy (when enabled for the API).
        --   git HTTP: OAuth2, access token, Actions tokens, integration JWT (basic too),
        --        reverse proxy.
        --   LFS: LFS token, OAuth2, access token (basic only), Actions task token (basic
        --        only), integration JWT, reverse proxy.
        --   web: reverse proxy (when enabled), session.
        -- A Basic header whose password is an account password is refused with 401
        -- "use a token" (decided: no password Basic auth).
}

surface ReverseProxyBoundary {
    facing proxy: TrustedReverseProxy

    provides:
        TrustedProxyAssertsUser(proxy, user, via_api)
            when config.enable_reverse_proxy_auth
        TrustedProxyRegistersUser(proxy, name, email, full_name)
            when config.enable_reverse_proxy_auth and config.enable_reverse_proxy_auto_registration
}

-- The callback leg of an external sign-in.
surface IdentityProviderCallback {
    facing provider: IdentityProvider

    context session: Session

    exposes:
        provider.name

    provides:
        ProviderReturnsIdentity(session, identity)

    @guidance
        -- /user/oauth2/{source}/callback. Supported providers include generic OpenID
        -- Connect (discovery URL), GitHub, GitLab, Gitea/Forgejo, Bitbucket, Nextcloud,
        -- Mastodon, Azure AD, Microsoft, Google, Discord, Twitter, Dropbox, Facebook,
        -- Yandex; self-hosted ones accept custom auth/token/profile/email URLs.
}

surface AuthSourceAdministration {
    facing admin: access/SiteAdmin

    exposes:
        for source in AuthSources:
            source.name
            source.kind
            source.is_active
            source.sync_enabled
            source.in_use
            source.created_at

    provides:
        AdminCreatesAuthSource(admin, name, kind, is_active, sync_enabled, settings)
        AdminUpdatesAuthSource(admin, source, name, is_active, sync_enabled, settings)
        AdminDeletesAuthSource(admin, source)
        OwnerRegistersOAuth2Application(admin, owner_user, owner_org, name, redirect_uris, confidential)
            when config.oauth2_enabled
        OwnerUpdatesOAuth2Application(admin, app, name, redirect_uris, confidential)
        OwnerDeletesOAuth2Application(admin, app)
        UserCreatesAccessToken(admin, owner, name, scopes, public_only, all_repositories, repositories, via)
        AdminRunsExternalUserSync(admin)

    timeout:
        ExternalUserSyncDue

    @guidance
        -- Web: /admin/auths, /admin/auths/new, /admin/auths/{id}, /admin/auths/{id}/delete,
        -- /admin/applications(/oauth2/{id}...). Admin dashboard: "synchronise external
        -- user data" runs ExternalUserSyncDue now. API: /admin/users/{username}/tokens.
}

-- The credential facts offered to every other module (password policy,
-- second factors, token scope categories, external-identity lookups).
surface AuthenticationService {
    facing component: access/ForgeInternals

    exposes:
        component.name
        config.min_password_length
        config.password_complexity
        config.password_check_pwned
        config.global_two_factor_requirement

    contracts:
        fulfils CredentialPolicy

    @guarantee AnswersFollowCurrentState
        -- has_two_factor, must_have_two_factor and the lookups reflect every
        -- enrolment, removal and link committed before the request.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Local black box: can_read_code(user, repository) is access/can_read(user, repository, code).
deferred AccessToken.enforcement           -- see: access.allium (scope/public-only/repository reducers per endpoint)
deferred ExternalGroupsAsserted.team_mapping -- see: organizations.allium (group_team_map, dynamic maps, removal)
deferred ExternalQuotaGroupsAsserted.quota_mapping -- see: quota.allium (quota_group_map)

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Requests to other modules
------------------------------------------------------------
-- REQUEST accounts/User.kind: individual | bot | ... — used to refuse password sign-in for non-individuals.
-- REQUEST accounts/username_available(name): black-box check covering syntax, reserved names (the fixed lists and every accounts/ReservedName, case-insensitive), cooldown, uniqueness.
-- REQUEST accounts/email_available(email): black-box uniqueness check across all addresses.
-- REQUEST accounts/user_count(): number of user accounts (first account becomes admin).
-- REQUEST accounts/user_by_email(email): the account holding this activated address, for account-link auto mode (decided: e-mail only, no name match).
-- REQUEST accounts: react to ExternalAvatarAsserted(user, url), ExternalAdminFlagsAsserted(user, is_admin, is_restricted).
-- REQUEST accounts: UserLogin is created by authentication for self-registration; administration's "admin creates user" must create a UserLogin (with must_change_password) too.
-- REQUEST organizations: react to ExternalGroupsAsserted(user, source, groups) per the source's group_team_map / dynamic maps; react to AuthSourceDeleted(source) by clearing membership provenance.
-- REQUEST keys/SshKey.owner: accounts/User — the key an HTTP signature is verified against; react to ExternalSshKeysAsserted(user, source, keys) (source-managed keys).
-- REQUEST access: consume RequestAuthenticated(user, method) and the token's scopes / public_only / repositories to reduce permissions; access/can_read(user, repository, unit).
-- REQUEST notifications: send mail for ActivationEmailRequested, EmailConfirmationRequested, PasswordResetRequested, PasswordChanged, TotpEnrolled, TotpDisabled, SecurityKeyRemoved; push "logout" on UserSignedOut.
